{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013U5oYALyB43vqg7SAHEiMx","type":"tool_result","content":"# Git Subtree: Merging Repos While Preserving History\n\nI apologize, but the provided content appears to be primarily CSS styling code and font definitions from an Atlassian web page, rather than actual documentation about git subtree functionality.\n\nTo properly answer your questions about:\n- How git subtree works for merging repositories\n- The process for using `git subtree add` to incorporate another repo's history\n\nI would need access to the actual tutorial or documentation text content, which isn't available in the source material you've provided.\n\n**Recommendation:** Please share the actual text content of the Atlassian Git Subtree tutorial rather than the page's styling markup. This will allow me to give you an accurate, properly cited response about git subtree's history-preserving capabilities and implementation steps."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6993f78a-29cd-45b5-8210-954a87e5df7f","uuid":"8eaeb900-1a60-4e9c-a417-ca84ce61f46b","tool_use_result":{"bytes":1704780,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Git Subtree: Merging Repos While Preserving History\n\nI apologize, but the provided content appears to be primarily CSS styling code and font definitions from an Atlassian web page, rather than actual documentation about git subtree functionality.\n\nTo properly answer your questions about:\n- How git subtree works for merging repositories\n- The process for using `git subtree add` to incorporate another repo's history\n\nI would need access to the actual tutorial or documentation text content, which isn't available in the source material you've provided.\n\n**Recommendation:** Please share the actual text content of the Atlassian Git Subtree tutorial rather than the page's styling markup. This will allow me to give you an accurate, properly cited response about git subtree's history-preserving capabilities