{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KuSvQFdm8EVYnRnhPTFinn","type":"tool_result","content":"# Git Subtree Merges Summary\n\n## Overview\nA subtree merge allows you to \"contain a repository within a repository\" by storing a subproject in a folder of your main repository while preserving its complete Git history.\n\n## Key Workflow\n\n**1. Add the remote repository:**\n```bash\ngit remote add -f spoon-knife https://github.com/octocat/Spoon-Knife.git\n```\n\n**2. Merge without committing** (prepare Git for the next step):\n- Git 2.9+: `git merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories spoon-knife/main`\n- Git 2.8 or earlier: `git merge -s ours --no-commit spoon-knife/main`\n\n**3. Copy the project into a subdirectory:**\n```bash\ngit read-tree --prefix=spoon-knife/ -u spoon-knife/main\n```\n\n**4. Commit the changes:**\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"Subtree merged in spoon-knife\"\n```\n\n## Keeping in Sync\nUpdate the subproject with: `git pull -s subtree REMOTE-NAME BRANCH-NAME`\n\nExample: `git pull -s subtree spoon-knife main`\n\n## Important Note\nRemotes added during setup won't persist in fresh clones—you'll need to re-add them using `git remote add`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6993f78a-29cd-45b5-8210-954a87e5df7f","uuid":"705712ce-e29f-44a9-a54f-024f0875f427","tool_use_result":{"bytes":170659,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Git Subtree Merges Summary\n\n## Overview\nA subtree merge allows you to \"contain a repository within a repository\" by storing a subproject in a folder of your main repository while preserving its complete Git history.\n\n## Key Workflow\n\n**1. Add the remote repository:**\n```bash\ngit remote add -f spoon-knife https://github.com/octocat/Spoon-Knife.git\n```\n\n**2. Merge without committing** (prepare Git for the next step):\n- Git 2.9+: `git merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories spoon-knife/main`\n- Git 2.8 or earlier: `git merge -s ours --no-commit spoon-knife/main`\n\n**3. Copy the project into a subdirectory:**\n```bash\ngit read-tree --prefix=spoon-knife/ -u spoon-knife/main\n```\n\n**4. Commit the changes:**\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"Subtree merged in spoon-knife\"\n```\n\n## Keeping in Sync\nUpdate the subproject with: `git pull -s subtree REMOTE-NAME BRANCH-NAME`\n\nExample: `git pull -s subtree spoon-knife main`\n\n## Important Note\nRemotes added during setup won't persist in fresh clones—you'll need to re-add them using `git remote add`.","durationMs":6246,"url":"https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/using-git/about-git-subtree-merges"},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:07:11.641Z"}
