{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KsgBLLuAjyPXNxwREnRDyv","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# What's New in Hankweave (Since January 16, 2026)\n     2→\n     3→**Analysis Period**: January 16 - February 5, 2026\n     4→**Version Jump**: 0.1.37 → 0.2.0\n     5→**Total Commits**: 200+ commits\n     6→**Major Features**: 15+\n     7→**Bug Fixes**: 50+\n     8→\n     9→This document comprehensively covers all changes, features, improvements, and behavioral modifications in Hankweave since January 16, 2026.\n    10→\n    11→---\n    12→\n    13→## Table of Contents\n    14→\n    15→1. [Major Features](#major-features)\n    16→2. [Quality of Life Improvements](#quality-of-life-improvements)\n    17→3. [Infrastructure & Platform Support](#infrastructure--platform-support)\n    18→4. [Bug Fixes](#bug-fixes)\n    19→5. [Breaking Changes](#breaking-changes)\n    20→6. [Configuration & Schema Changes](#configuration--schema-changes)\n    21→7. [CLI & Command Line Interface](#cli--command-line-interface)\n    22→8. [Developer Experience](#developer-experience)\n    23→9. [Performance & Optimization](#performance--optimization)\n    24→10. [Testing & CI/CD](#testing--cicd)\n    25→11. [Behavioral Changes](#behavioral-changes)\n    26→\n    27→---\n    28→\n    29→## Major Features\n    30→\n    31→### 1. OpenAI Codex Integration (v0.1.47, PR #77)\n    32→\n    33→**What it does**: Run codons using OpenAI models (GPT-4.1, GPT-5.2 variants) via the Codex CLI\n    34→\n    35→**Key Components**:\n    36→\n    37→- Platform-specific Codex binary extraction from `@openai/codex-sdk` package\n    38→- Automatic binary detection: uses `node_modules` in dev, extracts to `~/.hankweave/codex-sdk/<version>/` for compiled executables\n    39→- Self-test functionality verifies Codex installation and API key configuration\n    40→- Multiple auth methods: `~/.codex/auth.json`, `CODEX_API_KEY`, or `OPENAI_API_KEY` env vars\n    41→- New `codex-runtime-extractor.ts` module for embedded file extraction\n    42→- Reusable runtime extractor base shared across Claude SDK, Codex, and shim extractors\n    43→- Shim process manager updated to handle Codex-specific behaviors\n    44→\n    45→**Files Added/Modified**:\n    46→\n    47→- `server/codex-runtime-extractor.ts` (new)\n    48→- `server/runtime-extractor-base.ts` (new)\n    49→- `shims/codex/index.js` (new)\n    50→- `tests/integration/codex-shim.test.ts` (new)\n    51→- `tests/unit/codex-runtime-extractor.test.ts` (new)\n    52→\n    53→**Configuration**:\n    54→\n    55→- Use `\"model\": \"gpt-4.1\"` or any Codex-supported model in hank.json\n    56→- Auth configured via `~/.codex/auth.json` or environment variables\n    57→\n    58→### 2. Codon Failure Handling (v0.2.0, ENG-104, PR #86)\n    59→\n    60→**What it does**: Allow codons to continue executing even when they fail, with configurable failure policies\n    61→\n    62→**Failure Policies**:\n    63→\n    64→- **`abort`** (default): Current behavior, stops execution on failure\n    65→- **`retry`**: Retry the codon with configurable attempts\n    66→- **`ignore`**: Continue to next codon, treating failure as non-fatal\n    67→\n    68→**Configuration Example**:\n    69→\n    70→```json\n    71→{\n    72→  \"id\": \"optional-polish\",\n    73→  \"promptFile\": \"polish.md\",\n    74→  \"onFailure\": {\n    75→    \"action\": \"ignore\"\n    76→  }\n    77→}\n    78→```\n    79→\n    80→**Retry Configuration**:\n    81→\n    82→```json\n    83→{\n    84→  \"id\": \"flaky-task\",\n    85→  \"promptFile\": \"task.md\",\n    86→  \"onFailure\": {\n    87→    \"action\": \"retry\",\n    88→    \"maxRetries\": 3\n    89→  }\n    90→}\n    91→```\n    92→\n    93→**Key Behaviors**:\n    94→\n    95→- Failed-but-ignored codons emit special events for tracking\n    96→- Checkpoints still created for debugging\n    97→- Costs tracked for failed codons\n    98→- Compatible with existing sentinel `failCodonIfNotLoaded` pattern\n    99→- TUI displays ignored failures distinctly\n   100→\n   101→**Use Cases**:\n   102→\n   103→- Optional polishing steps (formatting, linting)\n   104→- Best-effort enhancements that might fail\n   105→- Non-critical operations (comments, documentation)\n   106→\n   107→**Files Modified**:\n   108→\n   109→- `server/config.ts` - Added `onFailure` schema\n   110→- `server/hankweave-runtime.ts` - Failure handling logic\n   111→- `server/types/state-types.ts` - New failure states\n   112→- `tests/e2e/test-groups/failure-policy-tests.ts` (new)\n   113→\n   114→### 3. Codon Extensions (\"Consuela Loop\") (v0.1.46+, ENG-13, PR #90)\n   115→\n   116→**What it does**: Allow a single codon to continue executing beyond its initial prompt until context is exhausted\n   117→\n   118→**Key Concept**: Unlike loops that create multiple codon instances, extensions keep it as ONE codon with multiple \"turns\"\n   119→\n   120→**Configuration**:\n   121→\n   122→```json\n   123→{\n   124→  \"id\": \"exhaustive-analysis\",\n   125→  \"promptFile\": \"analyze.md\",\n   126→  \"exhaustWithPrompt\": \"Please continue analyzing. Any more insights?\"\n   127→}\n   128→```\n   129→\n   130→**Behaviors**:\n   131→\n   132→- One `codon.completed` event (not one per iteration)\n   133→- One set of output files\n   134→- Sentinels fire once at true completion\n   135→- Rollback treats entire extended codon as single atomic unit\n   136→- Extension prompt automatically fed back to agent after each completion\n   137→- Continues until context exhausted or agent explicitly stops\n   138→\n   139→**Use Cases**:\n   140→\n   141→- Exhaustive analysis of large datasets\n   142→- Iterative refinement until context fills\n   143→- Documentation generation that uses maximum context\n   144→- Research tasks (\"tell me everything you can find\")\n   145→\n   146→**Mental Model**:\n   147→\n   148→> \"This codon runs until context is exhausted\" - not \"this is a loop with N iterations\"\n   149→\n   150→**Files Modified**:\n   151→\n   152→- `server/codon-runner.ts` - Extension logic\n   153→- `server/prompt-builder.ts` - Extension prompt handling\n   154→- `server/schemas/event-schemas.ts` - Extension events\n   155→- `tests/e2e/codon-extension-e2e.test.ts` (new)\n   156→\n   157→### 4. Agent Directory Separation & Rig Archiving (v0.2.0, ENG-89/ENG-149, PR #96)\n   158→\n   159→**What it does**: Restructures execution directory to separate agent workspace from system files, with archiving support\n   160→\n   161→**New Directory Structure**:\n   162→\n   163→```\n   164→execution-dir/\n   165→├── agentRoot/           # Agent's workspace (Git work tree)\n   166→│   └── [your files]     # Where agent does all work\n   167→├── rigArchive/          # Archived files after success\n   168→│   ├── codon-id/        # Archived files for specific codon\n   169→│   └── loop-id-N/       # Archived files for loop iteration N\n   170→└── .hankweave/          # Hidden system files\n   171→    ├── checkpoints/     # Git checkpoint repository\n   172→    ├── logs/            # System logs\n   173→    ├── sentinels/       # Sentinel state\n   174→    └── archive-manifest.json  # Tracks archived files\n   175→```\n   176→\n   177→**Archive Configuration**:\n   178→\n   179→```json\n   180→{\n   181→  \"id\": \"build-artifacts\",\n   182→  \"promptFile\": \"build.md\",\n   183→  \"archiveOnSuccess\": [\"build/**/*\", \"dist/**/*\"]\n   184→}\n   185→```\n   186→\n   187→**Key Behaviors**:\n   188→\n   189→- Files moved from `agentRoot/` to `rigArchive/<codonId>/` on success\n   190→- Loop archives create iteration-specific dirs: `rigArchive/<loopId>-<iteration>/`\n   191→- Rollback automatically restores archived files\n   192→- Archive manifest tracks all operations\n   193→- Template variables (`<%AGENT_ROOT%>`, `<%PROJECT_DIR%>`, `<%EXECUTION_DIR%>`) all resolve to `agentRoot/`\n   194→- Checkpoint git directory renamed from `.git` to `.hankweavecheckpoints` to prevent Git submodule detection\n   195→\n   196→**Events**:\n   197→\n   198→- `archive.completed` - Successful archive operation\n   199→- `archive.partial` - Partial archive (some files failed)\n   200→- `rollback.archiveRestore` - Files restored from archive\n   201→\n   202→**Files Modified**:\n   203→\n   204→- `server/archive-manifest.ts` (new)\n   205→- `server/hankweave-runtime.ts` - Archive orchestration\n   206→- `server/execution-setup.ts` - Directory structure setup\n   207→- `server/prompt-builder.ts` - Template variable resolution\n   208→\n   209→### 5. JSON Schema Support (v0.1.44, ENG-162/164, PR #84)\n   210→\n   211→**What it does**: Provides editor autocomplete, type checking, and validation for Hankweave configuration files\n   212→\n   213→**Schemas Provided**:\n   214→\n   215→- `hank.schema.json` - For hank.json (workflow configuration)\n   216→- `hankweave.schema.json` - For hankweave.json (runtime settings)\n   217→- `sentinel.schema.json` - For sentinel configuration files\n   218→\n   219→**How to Use**:\n   220→Add to top of your hank.json:\n   221→\n   222→```json\n   223→{\n   224→  \"$schema\": \"https://unpkg.com/@southbridgeai/hankweave@latest/schemas/hank.schema.json\",\n   225→  \"hank\": [ ... ]\n   226→}\n   227→```\n   228→\n   229→**Features**:\n   230→\n   231→- Auto-generated from Zod schemas via `bun run generate-schemas`\n   232→- `hankweave init` includes `$schema` in generated files\n   233→- Running or validating auto-adds `$schema` if missing\n   234→- Schemas served via unpkg CDN\n   235→- Works in VS Code, WebStorm, and other editors with JSON Schema support\n   236→- Hover documentation shows field descriptions\n   237→- Autocomplete suggests available options\n   238→- Validation errors show immediately in editor\n   239→\n   240→**Stable Input Hashing**:\n   241→\n   242→- Inline/stdin input now creates content-addressed files in `~/.hankweave-cache/inputs/`\n   243→- Same content produces same hash, enabling proper resume with `--execution`\n   244→- Previously, `--input \"text\"` created different hashes each run\n   245→\n   246→**New Flag**: `--ignore-data-mismatch`\n   247→\n   248→- Allows resuming executions when data has intentionally changed\n   249→- Shows warning but continues instead of failing\n   250→- Properly relinks `read_only_data_source` to new data\n   251→\n   252→**Files Added**:\n   253→\n   254→- `schemas/hank.schema.json` (new)\n   255→- `schemas/hankweave.schema.json` (new)\n   256→- `schemas/sentinel.schema.json` (new)\n   257→- `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` (new)\n   258→\n   259→### 6. ASCII Structure Visualization (v0.1.47, ENG-175)\n   260→\n   261→**What it does**: Visual tree diagram of hank structure in `--validate` mode and before execution\n   262→\n   263→**Example Output**:\n   264→\n   265→```\n   266→┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n   267→│ [1] setup-environment               │\n   268→│ prompts: 1 (45 lines)               │\n   269→│ model: claude-sonnet-4-20250514     │\n   270→└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n   271→                ↓\n   272→┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n   273→│ [2] analyze-codebase (loop)         │\n   274→│ iteration limit: 3                  │\n   275→│ ┌─────────────────────────────────┐ │\n   276→│ │ [2.1] collect-files             │ │\n   277→│ │ prompts: 2 (120 lines)          │ │\n   278→│ └─────────────────────────────────┘ │\n   279→│                ↓                     │\n   280→│ ┌─────────────────────────────────┐ │\n   281→│ │ [2.2] analyze-patterns          │ │\n   282→│ │ prompts: 1 (80 lines)           │ │\n   283→│ └─────────────────────────────────┘ │\n   284→└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n   285→                ↓\n   286→┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n   287→│ [3] generate-report                 │\n   288→│ prompts: 3 (200 lines)              │\n   289→│ model: claude-opus-4-20250514       │\n   290→└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n   291→```\n   292→\n   293→**Features**:\n   294→\n   295→- Hierarchical numbering: [1], [2], [2.1], [2.2], [3]\n   296→- Flow arrows (↓) showing execution order\n   297→- Rounded box corners and loop body boxes\n   298→- Color output in terminal (auto-disabled when piped)\n   299→- Prompt line counts for at-a-glance sizing\n   300→- Terminal-width-aware rendering\n   301→- Clear visual grouping for loops\n   302→\n   303→---\n   304→\n   305→## Quality of Life Improvements\n   306→\n   307→### CLI Attach Mode (v0.1.46, ENG-103)\n   308→\n   309→**What it does**: Connect TUI to an already-running server in read-only mode\n   310→\n   311→**Usage**:\n   312→\n   313→```bash\n   314→# Auto-detect from lock file\n   315→hankweave --attach\n   316→\n   317→# Specify port directly\n   318→hankweave --attach --port 8080\n   319→```\n   320→\n   321→**Behaviors**:\n   322→\n   323→- Reads port from execution directory's lock file\n   324→- Commands disabled in attach mode\n   325→- Press `q` to disconnect without stopping server\n   326→- Useful for monitoring long-running processes\n   327→- Multiple clients can attach to same server\n   328→\n   329→### Required Environment Variables Validation (v0.1.46, ENG-121)\n   330→\n   331→**What it does**: Declare required env vars in hank.json for fail-fast validation\n   332→\n   333→**Configuration**:\n   334→\n   335→```json\n   336→{\n   337→  \"requirements\": {\n   338→    \"env\": [\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\", \"DATABASE_URL\"]\n   339→  },\n   340→  \"hank\": [ ... ]\n   341→}\n   342→```\n   343→\n   344→**Behaviors**:\n   345→\n   346→- Validation runs during both `--validate` and normal startup\n   347→- Supports `HANKWEAVE_` prefix: `HANKWEAVE_API_KEY` satisfies requirement for `API_KEY`\n   348→- Clear error messages when vars missing\n   349→- Prevents discovering missing keys deep into execution\n   350→\n   351→### Global System Prompts (v0.1.46, ENG-122)\n   352→\n   353→**What it does**: Apply a system prompt to ALL codons in a hank\n   354→\n   355→**Configuration**:\n   356→\n   357→```json\n   358→{\n   359→  \"globalSystemPromptFile\": [\"global-rules.md\", \"coding-standards.md\"],\n   360→  \"globalSystemPromptText\": \"Always explain your reasoning.\",\n   361→  \"hank\": [ ... ]\n   362→}\n   363→```\n   364→\n   365→**Behaviors**:\n   366→\n   367→- Global prompt prepended before codon-specific system prompts\n   368→- Configure via file path(s) or inline text\n   369→- Useful for enforcing conventions across all codons\n   370→- Can specify multiple files (processed in order)\n   371→\n   372→### Rig Setup Visibility (v0.1.46, ENG-102)\n   373→\n   374→**What it does**: Emits info events for rig setup progress\n   375→\n   376→**Events Emitted**:\n   377→\n   378→- `info` event for rig setup start\n   379→- `info` events for per-operation progress\n   380→- `info` event for completion with duration and success/failure counts\n   381→\n   382→**TUI Display**:\n   383→\n   384→- Distinct styling for rig setup events\n   385→- Real-time progress indication\n   386→- Clear visibility when long-running operations occur\n   387→\n   388→**Prevents**: Anxiety from operations that look hung but are actually running\n   389→\n   390→### `--ignore-rig-failures` Flag (v0.1.46, ENG-119)\n   391→\n   392→**What it does**: Global override to treat all rig setup operations as `allowFailure: true`\n   393→\n   394→**Usage**:\n   395→\n   396→```bash\n   397→hankweave --execution ./my-run --ignore-rig-failures\n   398→```\n   399→\n   400→**Use Case**: Resume workflows where rig setup already partially completed\n   401→\n   402→### Directory-Aware Config Resolution (v0.1.46, ENG-139)\n   403→\n   404→**What it does**: Automatically find hank.json in specified directory\n   405→\n   406→**Before**:\n   407→\n   408→```bash\n   409→hankweave ./project/  # Looked in CWD, not ./project/\n   410→```\n   411→\n   412→**After**:\n   413→\n   414→```bash\n   415→hankweave ./project/  # Correctly finds ./project/hank.json\n   416→```\n   417→\n   418→**Behavior**: Data directories containing hank.json are auto-discovered\n   419→\n   420→### Symlink Handling in Output Files (v0.1.46, ENG-125)\n   421→\n   422→**What it does**: Preserve symlinks when copying output files\n   423→\n   424→**Fix**: Added `verbatimSymlinks: true` to `fs.promises.cp()`\n   425→\n   426→**Before**: Copying directories with `node_modules/.bin/` symlinks failed with `EINVAL` errors\n   427→\n   428→**After**: Symlinks preserved correctly during copy operations\n   429→\n   430→### HTML Comment Stripping in Prompts (Unreleased, ENG-158)\n   431→\n   432→**What it does**: Remove HTML comments from prompts before sending to LLM\n   433→\n   434→**Syntax**:\n   435→\n   436→```markdown\n   437→This instruction is sent to the agent.\n   438→\n   439→<!-- This is a comment for the prompt author, not for the agent.\n   440→It explains WHY this instruction exists. -->\n   441→\n   442→More instructions for the agent.\n   443→```\n   444→\n   445→**Behaviors**:\n   446→\n   447→- Comments (`<!-- ... -->`) automatically stripped\n   448→- Trailing newlines consumed to prevent blank line accumulation\n   449→- Applies to system prompts, user prompts, and template variable processing\n   450→- Useful for adding internal notes and documentation\n   451→\n   452→**Philosophy**: \"Prompts - like code - aren't always self-documenting\"\n   453→\n   454→### Output File Conflict Resolution (Unreleased, ENG-115)\n   455→\n   456→**What it does**: Automatic handling of filename collisions when copying output files\n   457→\n   458→**Behavior**:\n   459→\n   460→- Conflicting files renamed with format: `file_<counter>_<timestamp>.ext`\n   461→- Example: `report.pdf` → `report_1_1738678800.pdf`\n   462→- Preflight warnings shown when output directory non-empty\n   463→- Server emits info events with conflict details\n   464→- Safety limit of max 100 conflicts\n   465→\n   466→### Headless Autostart (Unreleased, ENG-180)\n   467→\n   468→**What it does**: Automatically start execution in headless mode without waiting for client\n   469→\n   470→**Behavior**:\n   471→\n   472→- New `requestAutostart()` method for idempotent triggering\n   473→- Prevents race condition where both headless startup and client handshake trigger autostart\n   474→- Smart exit codes: 0 for success/user shutdown, 1 for codon failure\n   475→\n   476→**Use Case**: CI/CD environments, cloud deployments, automated workflows\n   477→\n   478→### Dynamic Port Allocation (Unreleased, ENG-179)\n   479→\n   480→**What it does**: Default to OS-assigned port instead of hardcoded 7777\n   481→\n   482→**Configuration**:\n   483→\n   484→- Default port changed from 7777 to 0 (OS-assigned ephemeral port)\n   485→- Startup sequence reordered: WebSocket binds first, then proxy on `actualPort + 1`\n   486→- Lock file updated with actual ports after binding\n   487→- `start()` method returns actual port\n   488→- Proxy falls back to dynamic port if preferred port unavailable\n   489→\n   490→**Prevents**: Port conflicts when running multiple Hankweave instances\n   491→\n   492→**CLI Help Updated**: Reflects auto-selection behavior\n   493→\n   494→### Cleaner Startup Logs (Unreleased)\n   495→\n   496→**What changed**: Removed noisy debug output from startup\n   497→\n   498→**Before**:\n   499→\n   500→```\n   501→[MODULE] Loading config...\n   502→[MODULE] Initializing runtime...\n   503→[DEBUG] Calculating data signature...\n   504→```\n   505→\n   506→**After**:\n   507→\n   508→```\n   509→╭────────────────────────────────────────╮\n   510→│ Hankweave v0.2.0                       │\n   511→│ Platform: darwin-arm64                 │\n   512→│ Node: v20.11.0                         │\n   513→╰────────────────────────────────────────╯\n   514→\n   515→Execution: ~/hanks/my-project\n   516→Status: resuming\n   517→Config: hank.json\n   518→Claude SDK: v1.2.3\n   519→Codex SDK: v0.4.5\n   520→```\n   521→\n   522→**Improvements**:\n   523→\n   524→- Version and platform info in clean rounded box\n   525→- Execution info grouped together\n   526→- Paths shortened with `~` for home directory\n   527→- Suppressed verbose \"Calculating data signature...\" message\n   528→- SDK managers return structured info instead of printing directly\n   529→\n   530→---\n   531→\n   532→## Infrastructure & Platform Support\n   533→\n   534→### Windows Support (v0.1.47, PR #77)\n   535→\n   536→**What changed**: Comprehensive Windows compatibility fixes\n   537→\n   538→**Specific Fixes**:\n   539→\n   540→1. **File URL Parsing**: Use `fileURLToPath()` instead of manual parsing for cross-platform paths\n   541→2. **Path Duplication**: Fixed `path.join()` with absolute paths in `HankweaveRuntime` constructor\n   542→3. **Directory Cleanup**: Added `rmSyncWithRetry()` with exponential backoff for Windows file locks\n   543→4. **Build Script**: Replaced Unix commands (`cp -r`, `chmod`) with cross-platform Node.js APIs\n   544→5. **Double Extension**: Prevented `hankweave.exe.exe` on Windows builds\n   545→6. **NPX Discovery**: Set `NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` so npx finds `.npmrc` on Windows\n   546→7. **Codex on Windows**: Guide model to use `Write` tool instead of PowerShell commands\n   547→8. **Line Endings**: `.gitattributes` enforces LF line endings for text files\n   548→\n   549→**Testing**: Full test suite now runs on Windows in CI\n   550→\n   551→### Multi-OS CI Testing (v0.1.47, PR #77)\n   552→\n   553→**What changed**: CI now runs on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows\n   554→\n   555→**Features**:\n   556→\n   557→- E2E tests with retry logic for flaky network conditions\n   558→- Platform-specific test configurations\n   559→- Reusable composite actions:\n   560→  - `setup-environment` - Bun, Node.js, agent auth setup\n   561→  - `dump-test-logs` - Better CI debugging\n   562→- Codex auth via `~/.codex/auth.json` from CI secrets\n   563→- Extended timeouts for slower platforms (Windows)\n   564→\n   565→**Platforms Tested**:\n   566→\n   567→- Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04\n   568→- macOS 13 (Intel), 14 (Apple Silicon)\n   569→- Windows 2022, 2025\n   570→\n   571→### Runtime Extractor Refactor (v0.1.47, PR #77)\n   572→\n   573→**What changed**: Shared utilities for embedded file extraction across all runtime managers\n   574→\n   575→**New Base Extractor** (`runtime-extractor-base.ts`):\n   576→\n   577→- Handles Bun virtual filesystem paths correctly across platforms\n   578→- Shared caching logic\n   579→- Version management\n   580→- Platform detection\n   581→\n   582→**Refactored Extractors**:\n   583→\n   584→- `claude-runtime-extractor.ts`: Migrated to base (-215 lines)\n   585→- `shim-runtime-extractor.ts`: Migrated to base (-186 lines)\n   586→- `codex-runtime-extractor.ts`: New, using base\n   587→\n   588→**Benefits**: Consistency, reduced duplication, easier maintenance\n   589→\n   590→### Public Release Infrastructure (v0.1.41, PR #79)\n   591→\n   592→**What it does**: Automation for maintaining public/private repo split\n   593→\n   594→**Architecture**:\n   595→\n   596→- Two-repo model: private development, public release mirror\n   597→- `hankweave` npm package available publicly\n   598→- Sync workflow transforms private → clean public releases\n   599→- Internal files stripped from public:\n   600→  - `intermediates/` folder\n   601→  - `CLAUDE.md` file\n   602→  - Planning documents\n   603→  - Internal notes\n   604→\n   605→**Scripts**:\n   606→\n   607→- `scripts/sync-public.ts` - Sync and sanitize\n   608→- `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` - Test locally before pushing\n   609→\n   610→**CI Workflow**: `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`\n   611→\n   612→---\n   613→\n   614→## Bug Fixes\n   615→\n   616→### Critical Fixes\n   617→\n   618→#### Dynamic Port Display Bug (Unreleased)\n   619→\n   620→**Problem**: Banner showed `ws://localhost:0` instead of actual assigned port\n   621→**Impact**: TUI attempted to connect to port 0, causing immediate connection failure\n   622→**Fix**: Correctly read actual port from crossws Bun adapter via `.bun.server.port`\n   623→**Affects**: All dynamic port allocations (default behavior)\n   624→\n   625→#### HTTP Request Crash in Headless Mode (Unreleased)\n   626→\n   627→**Problem**: Server crashed when receiving HTTP requests (curl, browser, health checks)\n   628→**Error**: `fetchHandler is not a function`\n   629→**Fix**: Return helpful JSON error message directing users to WebSocket endpoint\n   630→**Impact**: Critical for CI/CD where stray HTTP probes could kill entire runs\n   631→**Added**: CORS headers for better browser compatibility\n   632→\n   633→#### Cost Counting Bug (Post-v0.2.0, ENG-181)\n   634→\n   635→**Problem**: Costs tracked incorrectly in certain scenarios\n   636→**Fix**: Proper cost aggregation and event handling\n   637→**Commit**: 8c2d64b\n   638→\n   639→### Sentinel Fixes\n   640→\n   641→#### Sentinel Output Path Resolution (Unreleased)\n   642→\n   643→**Problem**: Paths with `/` (including `./`) resolved incorrectly\n   644→**Before**: All explicit paths resolved relative to `executionPath` (outer directory)\n   645→**After**: Paths with `/` resolve relative to `agentRootPath` (agent workspace)\n   646→**Behavior**: Filename-only paths still use managed directory: `.hankweave/sentinels/outputs/{id}/`\n   647→**Allows**: Sentinels to write outputs directly to agent workspace (e.g., `./analysis.log`)\n   648→\n   649→### Windows-Specific Fixes (v0.1.47)\n   650→\n   651→1. **Self-test timeout handling**: Improved Windows cleanup and timeout behavior\n   652→2. **Directory cleanup**: Retry logic for Windows file locks\n   653→3. **Path handling**: Prevented Windows path duplication\n   654→4. **Binary extraction**: Detailed logging to diagnose issues\n   655→5. **Unit test failures**: Resolved Windows-specific unit test issues\n   656→6. **Integration test timeouts**: Increased timeouts for slower operations\n   657→\n   658→### Miscellaneous Fixes\n   659→\n   660→#### Loop Expansion with Ignored Early Failures\n   661→\n   662→**Problem**: Loop expansion broke when early codons failed with ignore policy\n   663→**Fix**: Proper handling of ignored failures in loop planning\n   664→\n   665→#### Log Parser Re-parsing Bug\n   666→\n   667→**Problem**: Log parser restarted on each extension, re-processing all previous messages\n   668→**Impact**: Duplicate cost tracking, incorrect state transitions\n   669→**Fix**: Log parser continues running across extensions\n   670→\n   671→#### successResultReceived Reset\n   672→\n   673→**Problem**: Flag not reset between extensions\n   674→**Impact**: Extension failures masked as successes when SDK errors occurred\n   675→**Fix**: Reset flag in `performExtension()` alongside other per-extension state\n   676→\n   677→#### NPX E2E Test Flakiness\n   678→\n   679→**Problem**: Flaky test failures in CI\n   680→**Fix**: Added retry logic (2 attempts), disabled npm update/audit checks\n   681→\n   682→---\n   683→\n   684→## Breaking Changes\n   685→\n   686→### Configuration Schema Changes\n   687→\n   688→#### `recommendations` → `overrides` (v0.1.44, PR #82)\n   689→\n   690→**Breaking**: Renamed field in hank.json\n   691→\n   692→**Before**:\n   693→\n   694→```json\n   695→{\n   696→  \"recommendations\": {\n   697→    \"model\": \"claude-opus-4\"\n   698→  }\n   699→}\n   700→```\n   701→\n   702→**After**:\n   703→\n   704→```json\n   705→{\n   706→  \"overrides\": {\n   707→    \"model\": \"claude-opus-4\"\n   708→  }\n   709→}\n   710→```\n   711→\n   712→**Migration**: Update all hank.json files to use `overrides` instead of `recommendations`\n   713→\n   714→#### Checkpoint Directory Rename (v0.2.0)\n   715→\n   716→**Breaking**: Checkpoint git directory renamed\n   717→\n   718→**Before**: `.git`\n   719→**After**: `.hankweavecheckpoints`\n   720→\n   721→**Reason**: Prevent Git submodule detection when committing execution environments\n   722→\n   723→**Migration**: Automatic! Existing execution environments migrated on startup\n   724→\n   725→#### Template Variable Resolution (v0.2.0)\n   726→\n   727→**Breaking**: All template variables now resolve to `agentRoot/`\n   728→\n   729→**Variables Affected**:\n   730→\n   731→- `<%AGENT_ROOT%>`\n   732→- `<%PROJECT_DIR%>`\n   733→- `<%EXECUTION_DIR%>`\n   734→\n   735→**Before**: Mix of resolutions depending on context\n   736→**After**: All consistently resolve to agent workspace\n   737→\n   738→**Impact**: Commands in rigSetup or outputFiles referencing these variables\n   739→\n   740→### Directory Structure Changes (v0.2.0)\n   741→\n   742→**Breaking**: Execution directory now nested\n   743→\n   744→**Before**:\n   745→\n   746→```\n   747→execution-dir/\n   748→├── .hankweave/\n   749→├── your-files\n   750→└── checkpoints/\n   751→```\n   752→\n   753→**After**:\n   754→\n   755→```\n   756→execution-dir/\n   757→├── agentRoot/     # Work happens here\n   758→│   └── your-files\n   759→├── rigArchive/    # Archives here\n   760→└── .hankweave/    # System files here\n   761→```\n   762→\n   763→**Migration**: Automatic migration on first v0.2.0 run\n   764→\n   765→**Impact**: External tools referencing execution directory structure\n   766→\n   767→### Deprecated Syntax\n   768→\n   769→#### CLI Flag Syntax (v0.1.34)\n   770→\n   771→**Not Breaking Yet**: Space-separated now preferred\n   772→\n   773→**Old Style** (still supported):\n   774→\n   775→```bash\n   776→hankweave --port=8080 --model=claude-opus-4\n   777→```\n   778→\n   779→**New Style** (recommended):\n   780→\n   781→```bash\n   782→hankweave --port 8080 --model claude-opus-4\n   783→```\n   784→\n   785→**Migration**: Update scripts to use space-separated flags\n   786→**Warning**: Deprecation warnings shown when using `--flag=value` syntax\n   787→\n   788→---\n   789→\n   790→## Configuration & Schema Changes\n   791→\n   792→### New Configuration Fields\n   793→\n   794→#### Codon-Level Fields\n   795→\n   796→**`onFailure`** (v0.2.0):\n   797→\n   798→```json\n   799→{\n   800→  \"onFailure\": {\n   801→    \"action\": \"abort\" | \"retry\" | \"ignore\",\n   802→    \"maxRetries\": 3  // For retry action\n   803→  }\n   804→}\n   805→```\n   806→\n   807→**`exhaustWithPrompt`** (v0.1.46+):\n   808→\n   809→```json\n   810→{\n   811→  \"exhaustWithPrompt\": \"Please continue. Any more?\"\n   812→}\n   813→```\n   814→\n   815→**`archiveOnSuccess`** (v0.2.0):\n   816→\n   817→```json\n   818→{\n   819→  \"archiveOnSuccess\": [\"build/**/*\", \"*.log\"]\n   820→}\n   821→```\n   822→\n   823→#### Hank-Level Fields\n   824→\n   825→**`requirements`** (v0.1.46):\n   826→\n   827→```json\n   828→{\n   829→  \"requirements\": {\n   830→    \"env\": [\"API_KEY\", \"DATABASE_URL\"]\n   831→  }\n   832→}\n   833→```\n   834→\n   835→**`globalSystemPromptFile`** (v0.1.46):\n   836→\n   837→```json\n   838→{\n   839→  \"globalSystemPromptFile\": [\"rules.md\", \"standards.md\"]\n   840→}\n   841→```\n   842→\n   843→**`globalSystemPromptText`** (v0.1.46):\n   844→\n   845→```json\n   846→{\n   847→  \"globalSystemPromptText\": \"Always explain reasoning.\"\n   848→}\n   849→```\n   850→\n   851→**`overrides`** (v0.1.44):\n   852→\n   853→```json\n   854→{\n   855→  \"overrides\": {\n   856→    \"model\": \"claude-opus-4\",\n   857→    \"maxTokens\": 8000\n   858→  }\n   859→}\n   860→```\n   861→\n   862→### Schema Files (v0.1.44)\n   863→\n   864→Three JSON Schema files now available:\n   865→\n   866→1. **`schemas/hank.schema.json`**\n   867→   - Defines hank.json structure\n   868→   - Includes all codon fields, loop fields, meta, overrides\n   869→   - Comprehensive descriptions and examples\n   870→\n   871→2. **`schemas/hankweave.schema.json`**\n   872→   - Defines hankweave.json (runtime config)\n   873→   - Includes server settings, environment config\n   874→   - Port, autostart, proxy settings\n   875→\n   876→3. **`schemas/sentinel.schema.json`**\n   877→   - Defines sentinel configuration\n   878→   - Trigger patterns, output handling\n   879→   - Lifecycle and structured output options\n   880→\n   881→### Model Support\n   882→\n   883→**Added**: OpenAI models via Codex\n   884→\n   885→- `gpt-4.1`\n   886→- `gpt-4.1-mini`\n   887→- `gpt-5.2`\n   888→- `gpt-5.2-preview`\n   889→- All o1/o3 models with reasoning effort prefixes (high/xhigh)\n   890→\n   891→**Existing**: Claude models\n   892→\n   893→- `claude-opus-4-20250514`\n   894→- `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`\n   895→- `claude-haiku-4-20250514`\n   896→- etc.\n   897→\n   898→**Existing**: Gemini models\n   899→\n   900→- `gemini-2.5-pro`\n   901→- `gemini-2.5-flash`\n   902→- etc.\n   903→\n   904→---\n   905→\n   906→## CLI & Command Line Interface\n   907→\n   908→### New Flags\n   909→\n   910→**`--attach`** (v0.1.46):\n   911→\n   912→- Connect TUI to running server in read-only mode\n   913→- Example: `hankweave --attach`\n   914→\n   915→**`--ignore-rig-failures`** (v0.1.46):\n   916→\n   917→- Treat all rig setup operations as allowFailure: true\n   918→- Example: `hankweave --execution ./my-run --ignore-rig-failures`\n   919→\n   920→**`--ignore-data-mismatch`** (v0.1.44):\n   921→\n   922→- Resume with changed data without failing\n   923→- Example: `hankweave --execution ./my-run --ignore-data-mismatch --data ./new-data`\n   924→\n   925→**`--version`** (v0.1.38):\n   926→\n   927→- Print version number without banner\n   928→- Example: `hankweave --version`\n   929→\n   930→### Modified Flags\n   931→\n   932→**`--port`** (Unreleased):\n   933→\n   934→- Default changed from 7777 to 0 (dynamic allocation)\n   935→- Explicit port still respected\n   936→\n   937→### Removed Flags\n   938→\n   939→**`-V`** (v0.1.37):\n   940→\n   941→- Removed to avoid confusion with `-v` (validation)\n   942→- Use `--version` instead\n   943→\n   944→### Improved Help Text\n   945→\n   946→**Changes**:\n   947→\n   948→- Better examples for all commands\n   949→- Clearer flag descriptions\n   950→- Positional argument documentation\n   951→- Remote URL usage examples\n   952→- Updated to reflect new features\n   953→\n   954→---\n   955→\n   956→## Developer Experience\n   957→\n   958→### Editor Support (v0.1.44)\n   959→\n   960→**JSON Schema Autocomplete**:\n   961→\n   962→- IntelliSense in VS Code, WebStorm, etc.\n   963→- Hover documentation for all fields\n   964→- Instant validation errors\n   965→- Type-aware suggestions\n   966→\n   967→**Setup**:\n   968→\n   969→```json\n   970→{\n   971→  \"$schema\": \"https://unpkg.com/@southbridgeai/hankweave@latest/schemas/hank.schema.json\"\n   972→}\n   973→```\n   974→\n   975→### Better Validation Messages (v0.1.44, PR #80)\n   976→\n   977→**What improved**: Runtime validation error messages\n   978→\n   979→**Before**:\n   980→\n   981→```\n   982→Error: Unknown field \"systemPromptFile\"\n   983→```\n   984→\n   985→**After**:\n   986→\n   987→```\n   988→Error in codon \"analyze-code\":\n   989→  Unknown field \"systemPromptFile\"\n   990→  Did you mean \"appendSystemPromptFile\"?\n   991→```\n   992→\n   993→**Features**:\n   994→\n   995→- Errors show codon ID and name for context\n   996→- \"Did you mean X?\" suggestions for typos\n   997→- Multiple errors shown together (not just first)\n   998→- Better context for nested errors\n   999→\n  1000→### Model Override Actually Works (v0.1.44, PR #81)\n  1001→\n  1002→**Problem**: `--model` CLI flag didn't actually override codon models\n  1003→\n  1004→**Fix**: Override applied at config loading before validation\n  1005→\n  1006→**Before**:\n  1007→\n  1008→```bash\n  1009→hankweave --model claude-opus-4  # Codons still used their configured models\n  1010→```\n  1011→\n  1012→**After**:\n  1013→\n  1014→```bash\n  1015→hankweave --model claude-opus-4  # All codons now use claude-opus-4\n  1016→```\n  1017→\n  1018→### Prompt Documentation (Unreleased, ENG-158)\n  1019→\n  1020→**Feature**: HTML comments in prompts\n  1021→\n  1022→**Benefit**: Document WHY instructions exist without sending to LLM\n  1023→\n  1024→**Example**:\n  1025→\n  1026→```markdown\n  1027→Please format all code using prettier.\n  1028→\n  1029→<!-- We require prettier because:\n  1030→     1. Team style guide mandates it\n  1031→     2. Reduces git diff noise\n  1032→     3. Historical context: Added after July 2025 team meeting -->\n  1033→\n  1034→Use 2-space indentation.\n  1035→```\n  1036→\n  1037→### Lock File Port Discovery (v0.1.46)\n  1038→\n  1039→**What changed**: Lock file now includes `port` field\n  1040→\n  1041→**Usage**: `--attach` mode reads port from lock file automatically\n  1042→\n  1043→**File**: `.hankweave/lock.json`\n  1044→\n  1045→```json\n  1046→{\n  1047→  \"pid\": 12345,\n  1048→  \"port\": 54321,\n  1049→  \"version\": \"0.2.0\"\n  1050→}\n  1051→```\n  1052→\n  1053→---\n  1054→\n  1055→## Performance & Optimization\n  1056→\n  1057→### Test Runner Optimization (Post-v0.2.0)\n  1058→\n  1059→**What changed**: New test runner implementation\n  1060→\n  1061→**Performance**:\n  1062→\n  1063→- **Before**: 9+ minutes for full test suite\n  1064→- **After**: ~3 minutes for full test suite\n  1065→- **Improvement**: 3x faster\n  1066→\n  1067→**Changes**:\n  1068→\n  1069→- Parallel test execution\n  1070→- Better test isolation\n  1071→- Reduced setup/teardown overhead\n  1072→\n  1073→### Gemini Timeout Adjustments (v0.1.46+)\n  1074→\n  1075→**What changed**: Increased timeouts for Gemini API\n  1076→\n  1077→**Reason**: Gemini is slower than Claude for some operations\n  1078→\n  1079→**Impact**: More reliable tests, fewer flaky failures\n  1080→\n  1081→### Build Performance (v0.1.44)\n  1082→\n  1083→**What changed**: Schema generation integrated into build\n  1084→\n  1085→**Process**:\n  1086→\n  1087→```bash\n  1088→bun run generate-schemas  # Auto-generates from Zod\n  1089→bun run build            # Builds with fresh schemas\n  1090→```\n  1091→\n  1092→**Benefit**: Schemas always in sync with code\n  1093→\n  1094→---\n  1095→\n  1096→## Testing & CI/CD\n  1097→\n  1098→### E2E Test Coverage\n  1099→\n  1100→**New Test Suites**:\n  1101→\n  1102→1. **Failure Policy Tests** (`tests/e2e/test-groups/failure-policy-tests.ts`):\n  1103→   - Test abort, retry, ignore policies\n  1104→   - Verify state transitions\n  1105→   - Check event emissions\n  1106→\n  1107→2. **Codon Extension Tests** (`tests/e2e/codon-extension-e2e.test.ts`):\n  1108→   - Test extension mechanism\n  1109→   - Verify single completion event\n  1110→   - Test rollback behavior\n  1111→   - Validate state management\n  1112→\n  1113→3. **Codex Integration Tests** (`tests/integration/codex-shim.test.ts`):\n  1114→   - Test Codex binary extraction\n  1115→   - Verify auth methods\n  1116→   - Test self-test functionality\n  1117→   - Platform-specific behaviors\n  1118→\n  1119→4. **Data Mismatch Tests** (`tests/e2e/data-mismatch-ignore-flag-e2e.test.ts`):\n  1120→   - Test `--ignore-data-mismatch` flag\n  1121→   - Verify data relinking\n  1122→   - Check warning messages\n  1123→\n  1124→### Unit Test Additions\n  1125→\n  1126→**New Test Files**:\n  1127→\n  1128→- `tests/unit/codex-runtime-extractor.test.ts` (469 lines)\n  1129→- `tests/unit/extension-config.test.ts` (318 lines)\n  1130→- `tests/unit/extension-decision.test.ts` (173 lines)\n  1131→- `tests/unit/codon-failure-reason.test.ts` (67 lines)\n  1132→- `tests/unit/on-failure-config.test.ts` (253 lines)\n  1133→- `tests/unit/llm-provider-registry.test.ts` (390 lines)\n  1134→- `tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts` (275 lines)\n  1135→- `tests/unit/stable-input-path.test.ts` (139 lines)\n  1136→- `tests/integration/schema-zod-parity.test.ts` (227 lines)\n  1137→\n  1138→### CI/CD Improvements\n  1139→\n  1140→**Platform Matrix**:\n  1141→\n  1142→- Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04\n  1143→- macOS 13 (Intel), 14 (Apple Silicon)\n  1144→- Windows Server 2022, 2025\n  1145→\n  1146→**Reliability**:\n  1147→\n  1148→- Retry logic for flaky tests\n  1149→- Extended timeouts for slow platforms\n  1150→- Better log dumping for debugging\n  1151→- Conditional test execution per platform\n  1152→\n  1153→**Workflows**:\n  1154→\n  1155→- CI on every push/PR to develop and release/alpha\n  1156→- Automated schema generation before releases\n  1157→- Public sync workflow for release branches\n  1158→- Comprehensive E2E, integration, and unit test runs\n  1159→\n  1160→---\n  1161→\n  1162→## Behavioral Changes\n  1163→\n  1164→### Startup Behavior\n  1165→\n  1166→**Before v0.2.0**:\n  1167→\n  1168→1. Create execution directory\n  1169→2. Start WebSocket server on port 7777\n  1170→3. Wait for client to connect and handshake\n  1171→4. Autostart after handshake (if enabled)\n  1172→\n  1173→**After v0.2.0**:\n  1174→\n  1175→1. Create execution directory with new structure (agentRoot/, rigArchive/, .hankweave/)\n  1176→2. Start WebSocket server on dynamic port (or specified port)\n  1177→3. In headless mode: autostart immediately\n  1178→4. In normal mode: wait for client handshake\n  1179→\n  1180→### Checkpoint Behavior\n  1181→\n  1182→**Directory**: Changed from `.git` to `.hankweavecheckpoints`\n  1183→\n  1184→**Archiving Integration**:\n  1185→\n  1186→- Rolling back now restores archived files\n  1187→- Archive manifest updated during checkpoint operations\n  1188→- Empty archive directories cleaned up\n  1189→\n  1190→### Model Selection\n  1191→\n  1192→**Override Precedence** (v0.1.44):\n  1193→\n  1194→1. CLI `--model` flag (highest)\n  1195→2. `overrides.model` in hank.json\n  1196→3. Codon-specific `model` field\n  1197→4. Runtime config `model`\n  1198→5. Default model (lowest)\n  1199→\n  1200→**Previously**: Codon model couldn't be overridden by CLI flag\n  1201→\n  1202→### Execution Flow\n  1203→\n  1204→**Extensions** (v0.1.46+):\n  1205→\n  1206→- Codons with `exhaustWithPrompt` continue until context exhausted\n  1207→- Single codon ID throughout (no iteration numbers)\n  1208→- Events emitted once at true completion\n  1209→- Rollback reverts entire extended codon\n  1210→\n  1211→**Failure Handling** (v0.2.0):\n  1212→\n  1213→- Codons can continue after failure based on `onFailure` policy\n  1214→- Failed-but-ignored codons don't stop execution\n  1215→- Retry policy automatically re-attempts failed codons\n  1216→\n  1217→### Directory Resolution\n  1218→\n  1219→**Template Variables** (v0.2.0):\n  1220→All now resolve to `agentRoot/`:\n  1221→\n  1222→- `<%AGENT_ROOT%>`\n  1223→- `<%PROJECT_DIR%>`\n  1224→- `<%EXECUTION_DIR%>`\n  1225→\n  1226→**Config Path Discovery** (v0.1.46):\n  1227→\n  1228→- `hankweave ./folder/` now correctly looks for `./folder/hank.json`\n  1229→- Previously looked in current working directory\n  1230→\n  1231→### Output Handling\n  1232→\n  1233→**File Conflicts** (Unreleased):\n  1234→\n  1235→- Conflicting files automatically renamed with counter and timestamp\n  1236→- Preflight warnings for non-empty output directories\n  1237→- Info events emitted with conflict details\n  1238→\n  1239→**Sentinel Outputs** (Unreleased):\n  1240→\n  1241→- Paths with `/` resolve relative to `agentRoot/`\n  1242→- Filename-only paths use managed directory\n  1243→\n  1244→### Validation Behavior\n  1245→\n  1246→**Required Environment Variables** (v0.1.46):\n  1247→\n  1248→- Checked during `--validate` and normal startup\n  1249→- Supports `HANKWEAVE_` prefix variants\n  1250→- Fails fast with clear error messages\n  1251→\n  1252→**Schema Validation** (v0.1.44):\n  1253→\n  1254→- Better error messages with suggestions\n  1255→- Multiple errors reported together\n  1256→- Context included (codon ID, name)\n  1257→\n  1258→---\n  1259→\n  1260→## Summary Statistics\n  1261→\n  1262→### Version Progression\n  1263→\n  1264→- **Starting Version**: 0.1.37 (Jan 16, 2026)\n  1265→- **Ending Version**: 0.2.0 (Feb 5, 2026)\n  1266→- **Major Version Bump**: YES (0.1 → 0.2)\n  1267→- **Releases**: 12 releases in ~20 days\n  1268→\n  1269→### Code Changes\n  1270→\n  1271→- **Total Commits**: 200+ commits\n  1272→- **Major Features**: 15+ features\n  1273→- **Bug Fixes**: 50+ fixes\n  1274→- **Files Changed**: 500+ files modified/added\n  1275→- **Lines of Code**: ~50,000 lines added\n  1276→\n  1277→### Feature Breakdown\n  1278→\n  1279→- **Major Features**: 6 (Codex, Failure Handling, Extensions, Directory Separation, JSON Schema, ASCII Viz)\n  1280→- **QoL Improvements**: 15+\n  1281→- **Infrastructure Improvements**: 5 (Windows support, CI/CD, refactoring, public release)\n  1282→- **Bug Fixes**: 50+\n  1283→\n  1284→### Testing\n  1285→\n  1286→- **New E2E Tests**: 10+ test suites\n  1287→- **New Unit Tests**: 15+ test files\n  1288→- **Test Performance**: 3x faster (9min → 3min)\n  1289→- **Platform Coverage**: 3 OS, 6 platform variants\n  1290→\n  1291→### Documentation\n  1292→\n  1293→- **CHANGELOG Entries**: ~300 lines of changes documented\n  1294→- **Planning Documents**: 8 major feature plans\n  1295→- **JSON Schemas**: 3 comprehensive schemas\n  1296→\n  1297→---\n  1298→\n  1299→## Migration Guide\n  1300→\n  1301→### Upgrading from v0.1.x to v0.2.0\n  1302→\n  1303→#### 1. Update Configuration Files\n  1304→\n  1305→**Rename `recommendations` to `overrides`**:\n  1306→\n  1307→```bash\n  1308→# In all hank.json files:\n  1309→sed -i 's/\"recommendations\"/\"overrides\"/g' **/*.json\n  1310→```\n  1311→\n  1312→**Add JSON Schema (optional but recommended)**:\n  1313→\n  1314→```json\n  1315→{\n  1316→  \"$schema\": \"https://unpkg.com/@southbridgeai/hankweave@latest/schemas/hank.schema.json\",\n  1317→  ...\n  1318→}\n  1319→```\n  1320→\n  1321→#### 2. Update Scripts\n  1322→\n  1323→**Change CLI flag syntax**:\n  1324→\n  1325→```bash\n  1326→# Old\n  1327→hankweave --port=8080 --model=claude-opus-4\n  1328→\n  1329→# New\n  1330→hankweave --port 8080 --model claude-opus-4\n  1331→```\n  1332→\n  1333→**Update port references**:\n  1334→\n  1335→- Change hardcoded port 7777 references\n  1336→- Use dynamic port discovery or specify explicitly\n  1337→\n  1338→#### 3. Test Execution\n  1339→\n  1340→**Run validation first**:\n  1341→\n  1342→```bash\n  1343→hankweave --validate\n  1344→```\n  1345→\n  1346→**Check for directory migration**:\n  1347→\n  1348→```bash\n  1349→# Old structure still works - auto-migrated\n  1350→ls execution-dir/.git  # Becomes .hankweavecheckpoints\n  1351→\n  1352→# New structure created automatically\n  1353→ls execution-dir/agentRoot/\n  1354→ls execution-dir/rigArchive/\n  1355→ls execution-dir/.hankweave/\n  1356→```\n  1357→\n  1358→#### 4. Update External Tools\n  1359→\n  1360→**If accessing execution directory**:\n  1361→\n  1362→- Update paths from `execution-dir/` to `execution-dir/agentRoot/`\n  1363→- System files now in `execution-dir/.hankweave/`\n  1364→- Archives in `execution-dir/rigArchive/`\n  1365→\n  1366→#### 5. Optional: Use New Features\n  1367→\n  1368→**Add failure handling**:\n  1369→\n  1370→```json\n  1371→{\n  1372→  \"id\": \"optional-task\",\n  1373→  \"promptFile\": \"task.md\",\n  1374→  \"onFailure\": {\n  1375→    \"action\": \"ignore\"\n  1376→  }\n  1377→}\n  1378→```\n  1379→\n  1380→**Add exhaustion extensions**:\n  1381→\n  1382→```json\n  1383→{\n  1384→  \"id\": \"exhaustive-task\",\n  1385→  \"promptFile\": \"task.md\",\n  1386→  \"exhaustWithPrompt\": \"Please continue.\"\n  1387→}\n  1388→```\n  1389→\n  1390→**Add archiving**:\n  1391→\n  1392→```json\n  1393→{\n  1394→  \"id\": \"build-task\",\n  1395→  \"promptFile\": \"build.md\",\n  1396→  \"archiveOnSuccess\": [\"build/**/*\"]\n  1397→}\n  1398→```\n  1399→\n  1400→### Deprecation Warnings\n  1401→\n  1402→**Monitor for warnings**:\n  1403→\n  1404→- `--flag=value` syntax (use `--flag value` instead)\n  1405→- Old checkpoint directory (auto-migrated)\n  1406→\n  1407→### Getting Help\n  1408→\n  1409→**Documentation**: See updated docs at [docs location]\n  1410→**Issues**: Report bugs at [repo URL]\n  1411→**Community**: [Discord/forum link if available]\n  1412→\n  1413→---\n  1414→\n  1415→## Conclusion\n  1416→\n  1417→Hankweave has undergone significant maturation since January 16, 2026. The jump from v0.1.37 to v0.2.0 represents a major milestone in the project's evolution from prototype to production-ready tool.\n  1418→\n  1419→### Key Themes\n  1420→\n  1421→1. **Resilience**: Failure handling and extensions make workflows more robust\n  1422→2. **Cross-Platform**: Full Windows, macOS, Linux support\n  1423→3. **Developer Experience**: JSON Schema, better validation, cleaner UI\n  1424→4. **Flexibility**: Dynamic ports, headless mode, attach mode\n  1425→5. **Observability**: Better logging, events, visualization\n  1426→\n  1427→### Looking Forward\n  1428→\n  1429→The v0.2.0 release establishes a solid foundation for:\n  1430→\n  1431→- More complex agentic workflows\n  1432→- Production deployments\n  1433→- Team collaboration\n  1434→- Cross-platform development\n  1435→\n  1436→With comprehensive testing, clear documentation, and robust infrastructure, Hankweave is ready for real-world usage at scale.\n  1437→\n  1438→---\n  1439→\n  1440→**Document Version**: 1.0\n  1441→**Analysis Date**: February 5, 2026\n  1442→**Hankweave Version**: 0.2.0\n  1443→**Analysis Scope**: Changes since January 16, 2026\n  1444→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6993f78a-29cd-45b5-8210-954a87e5df7f","uuid":"01d7b208-2b3a-4492-b6c8-cf233ec663ef","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave-docs/notes/changes-jan-16-to-5-Feb.md","content":"# What's New in Hankweave (Since January 16, 2026)\n\n**Analysis Period**: January 16 - February 5, 2026\n**Version Jump**: 0.1.37 → 0.2.0\n**Total Commits**: 200+ commits\n**Major Features**: 15+\n**Bug Fixes**: 50+\n\nThis document comprehensively covers all changes, features, improvements, and behavioral modifications in Hankweave since January 16, 2026.\n\n---\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [Major Features](#major-features)\n2. [Quality of Life Improvements](#quality-of-life-improvements)\n3. [Infrastructure & Platform Support](#infrastructure--platform-support)\n4. [Bug Fixes](#bug-fixes)\n5. [Breaking Changes](#breaking-changes)\n6. [Configuration & Schema Changes](#configuration--schema-changes)\n7. [CLI & Command Line Interface](#cli--command-line-interface)\n8. [Developer Experience](#developer-experience)\n9. [Performance & Optimization](#performance--optimization)\n10. [Testing & CI/CD](#testing--cicd)\n11. [Behavioral Changes](#behavioral-changes)\n\n---\n\n## Major Features\n\n### 1. OpenAI Codex Integration (v0.1.47, PR #77)\n\n**What it does**: Run codons using OpenAI models (GPT-4.1, GPT-5.2 variants) via the Codex CLI\n\n**Key Components**:\n\n- Platform-specific Codex binary extraction from `@openai/codex-sdk` package\n- Automatic binary detection: uses `node_modules` in dev, extracts to `~/.hankweave/codex-sdk/<version>/` for compiled executables\n- Self-test functionality verifies Codex installation and API key configuration\n- Multiple auth methods: `~/.codex/auth.json`, `CODEX_API_KEY`, or `OPENAI_API_KEY` env vars\n- New `codex-runtime-extractor.ts` module for embedded file extraction\n- Reusable runtime extractor base shared across Claude SDK, Codex, and shim extractors\n- Shim process manager updated to handle Codex-specific behaviors\n\n**Files Added/Modified**:\n\n- `server/codex-runtime-extractor.ts` (new)\n- `server/runtime-extractor-base.ts` (new)\n- `shims/codex/index.js` (new)\n- `tests/integration/codex-shim.test.ts` (new)\n- `tests/unit/codex-runtime-extractor.test.ts` (new)\n\n**Configuration**:\n\n- Use `\"model\": \"gpt-4.1\"` or any Codex-supported model in hank.json\n- Auth configured via `~/.codex/auth.json` or environment variables\n\n### 2. Codon Failure Handling (v0.2.0, ENG-104, PR #86)\n\n**What it does**: Allow codons to continue executing even when they fail, with configurable failure policies\n\n**Failure Policies**:\n\n- **`abort`** (default): Current behavior, stops execution on failure\n- **`retry`**: Retry the codon with configurable attempts\n- **`ignore`**: Continue to next codon, treating failure as non-fatal\n\n**Configuration Example**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"optional-polish\",\n  \"promptFile\": \"polish.md\",\n  \"onFailure\": {\n    \"action\": \"ignore\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Retry Configuration**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"flaky-task\",\n  \"promptFile\": \"task.md\",\n  \"onFailure\": {\n    \"action\": \"retry\",\n    \"maxRetries\": 3\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Key Behaviors**:\n\n- Failed-but-ignored codons emit special events for tracking\n- Checkpoints still created for debugging\n- Costs tracked for failed codons\n- Compatible with existing sentinel `failCodonIfNotLoaded` pattern\n- TUI displays ignored failures distinctly\n\n**Use Cases**:\n\n- Optional polishing steps (formatting, linting)\n- Best-effort enhancements that might fail\n- Non-critical operations (comments, documentation)\n\n**Files Modified**:\n\n- `server/config.ts` - Added `onFailure` schema\n- `server/hankweave-runtime.ts` - Failure handling logic\n- `server/types/state-types.ts` - New failure states\n- `tests/e2e/test-groups/failure-policy-tests.ts` (new)\n\n### 3. Codon Extensions (\"Consuela Loop\") (v0.1.46+, ENG-13, PR #90)\n\n**What it does**: Allow a single codon to continue executing beyond its initial prompt until context is exhausted\n\n**Key Concept**: Unlike loops that create multiple codon instances, extensions keep it as ONE codon with multiple \"turns\"\n\n**Configuration**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"exhaustive-analysis\",\n  \"promptFile\": \"analyze.md\",\n  \"exhaustWithPrompt\": \"Please continue analyzing. Any more insights?\"\n}\n```\n\n**Behaviors**:\n\n- One `codon.completed` event (not one per iteration)\n- One set of output files\n- Sentinels fire once at true completion\n- Rollback treats entire extended codon as single atomic unit\n- Extension prompt automatically fed back to agent after each completion\n- Continues until context exhausted or agent explicitly stops\n\n**Use Cases**:\n\n- Exhaustive analysis of large datasets\n- Iterative refinement until context fills\n- Documentation generation that uses maximum context\n- Research tasks (\"tell me everything you can find\")\n\n**Mental Model**:\n\n> \"This codon runs until context is exhausted\" - not \"this is a loop with N iterations\"\n\n**Files Modified**:\n\n- `server/codon-runner.ts` - Extension logic\n- `server/prompt-builder.ts` - Extension prompt handling\n- `server/schemas/event-schemas.ts` - Extension events\n- `tests/e2e/codon-extension-e2e.test.ts` (new)\n\n### 4. Agent Directory Separation & Rig Archiving (v0.2.0, ENG-89/ENG-149, PR #96)\n\n**What it does**: Restructures execution directory to separate agent workspace from system files, with archiving support\n\n**New Directory Structure**:\n\n```\nexecution-dir/\n├── agentRoot/           # Agent's workspace (Git work tree)\n│   └── [your files]     # Where agent does all work\n├── rigArchive/          # Archived files after success\n│   ├── codon-id/        # Archived files for specific codon\n│   └── loop-id-N/       # Archived files for loop iteration N\n└── .hankweave/          # Hidden system files\n    ├── checkpoints/     # Git checkpoint repository\n    ├── logs/            # System logs\n    ├── sentinels/       # Sentinel state\n    └── archive-manifest.json  # Tracks archived files\n```\n\n**Archive Configuration**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"build-artifacts\",\n  \"promptFile\": \"build.md\",\n  \"archiveOnSuccess\": [\"build/**/*\", \"dist/**/*\"]\n}\n```\n\n**Key Behaviors**:\n\n- Files moved from `agentRoot/` to `rigArchive/<codonId>/` on success\n- Loop archives create iteration-specific dirs: `rigArchive/<loopId>-<iteration>/`\n- Rollback automatically restores archived files\n- Archive manifest tracks all operations\n- Template variables (`<%AGENT_ROOT%>`, `<%PROJECT_DIR%>`, `<%EXECUTION_DIR%>`) all resolve to `agentRoot/`\n- Checkpoint git directory renamed from `.git` to `.hankweavecheckpoints` to prevent Git submodule detection\n\n**Events**:\n\n- `archive.completed` - Successful archive operation\n- `archive.partial` - Partial archive (some files failed)\n- `rollback.archiveRestore` - Files restored from archive\n\n**Files Modified**:\n\n- `server/archive-manifest.ts` (new)\n- `server/hankweave-runtime.ts` - Archive orchestration\n- `server/execution-setup.ts` - Directory structure setup\n- `server/prompt-builder.ts` - Template variable resolution\n\n### 5. JSON Schema Support (v0.1.44, ENG-162/164, PR #84)\n\n**What it does**: Provides editor autocomplete, type checking, and validation for Hankweave configuration files\n\n**Schemas Provided**:\n\n- `hank.schema.json` - For hank.json (workflow configuration)\n- `hankweave.schema.json` - For hankweave.json (runtime settings)\n- `sentinel.schema.json` - For sentinel configuration files\n\n**How to Use**:\nAdd to top of your hank.json:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://unpkg.com/@southbridgeai/hankweave@latest/schemas/hank.schema.json\",\n  \"hank\": [ ... ]\n}\n```\n\n**Features**:\n\n- Auto-generated from Zod schemas via `bun run generate-schemas`\n- `hankweave init` includes `$schema` in generated files\n- Running or validating auto-adds `$schema` if missing\n- Schemas served via unpkg CDN\n- Works in VS Code, WebStorm, and other editors with JSON Schema support\n- Hover documentation shows field descriptions\n- Autocomplete suggests available options\n- Validation errors show immediately in editor\n\n**Stable Input Hashing**:\n\n- Inline/stdin input now creates content-addressed files in `~/.hankweave-cache/inputs/`\n- Same content produces same hash, enabling proper resume with `--execution`\n- Previously, `--input \"text\"` created different hashes each run\n\n**New Flag**: `--ignore-data-mismatch`\n\n- Allows resuming executions when data has intentionally changed\n- Shows warning but continues instead of failing\n- Properly relinks `read_only_data_source` to new data\n\n**Files Added**:\n\n- `schemas/hank.schema.json` (new)\n- `schemas/hankweave.schema.json` (new)\n- `schemas/sentinel.schema.json` (new)\n- `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` (new)\n\n### 6. ASCII Structure Visualization (v0.1.47, ENG-175)\n\n**What it does**: Visual tree diagram of hank structure in `--validate` mode and before execution\n\n**Example Output**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ [1] setup-environment               │\n│ prompts: 1 (45 lines)               │\n│ model: claude-sonnet-4-20250514     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n                ↓\n┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ [2] analyze-codebase (loop)         │\n│ iteration limit: 3                  │\n│ ┌─────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ [2.1] collect-files             │ │\n│ │ prompts: 2 (120 lines)          │ │\n│ └─────────────────────────────────┘ │\n│                ↓                     │\n│ ┌─────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ [2.2] analyze-patterns          │ │\n│ │ prompts: 1 (80 lines)           │ │\n│ └─────────────────────────────────┘ │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n                ↓\n┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ [3] generate-report                 │\n│ prompts: 3 (200 lines)              │\n│ model: claude-opus-4-20250514       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Features**:\n\n- Hierarchical numbering: [1], [2], [2.1], [2.2], [3]\n- Flow arrows (↓) showing execution order\n- Rounded box corners and loop body boxes\n- Color output in terminal (auto-disabled when piped)\n- Prompt line counts for at-a-glance sizing\n- Terminal-width-aware rendering\n- Clear visual grouping for loops\n\n---\n\n## Quality of Life Improvements\n\n### CLI Attach Mode (v0.1.46, ENG-103)\n\n**What it does**: Connect TUI to an already-running server in read-only mode\n\n**Usage**:\n\n```bash\n# Auto-detect from lock file\nhankweave --attach\n\n# Specify port directly\nhankweave --attach --port 8080\n```\n\n**Behaviors**:\n\n- Reads port from execution directory's lock file\n- Commands disabled in attach mode\n- Press `q` to disconnect without stopping server\n- Useful for monitoring long-running processes\n- Multiple clients can attach to same server\n\n### Required Environment Variables Validation (v0.1.46, ENG-121)\n\n**What it does**: Declare required env vars in hank.json for fail-fast validation\n\n**Configuration**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"requirements\": {\n    \"env\": [\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\", \"DATABASE_URL\"]\n  },\n  \"hank\": [ ... ]\n}\n```\n\n**Behaviors**:\n\n- Validation runs during both `--validate` and normal startup\n- Supports `HANKWEAVE_` prefix: `HANKWEAVE_API_KEY` satisfies requirement for `API_KEY`\n- Clear error messages when vars missing\n- Prevents discovering missing keys deep into execution\n\n### Global System Prompts (v0.1.46, ENG-122)\n\n**What it does**: Apply a system prompt to ALL codons in a hank\n\n**Configuration**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"globalSystemPromptFile\": [\"global-rules.md\", \"coding-standards.md\"],\n  \"globalSystemPromptText\": \"Always explain your reasoning.\",\n  \"hank\": [ ... ]\n}\n```\n\n**Behaviors**:\n\n- Global prompt prepended before codon-specific system prompts\n- Configure via file path(s) or inline text\n- Useful for enforcing conventions across all codons\n- Can specify multiple files (processed in order)\n\n### Rig Setup Visibility (v0.1.46, ENG-102)\n\n**What it does**: Emits info events for rig setup progress\n\n**Events Emitted**:\n\n- `info` event for rig setup start\n- `info` events for per-operation progress\n- `info` event for completion with duration and success/failure counts\n\n**TUI Display**:\n\n- Distinct styling for rig setup events\n- Real-time progress indication\n- Clear visibility when long-running operations occur\n\n**Prevents**: Anxiety from operations that look hung but are actually running\n\n### `--ignore-rig-failures` Flag (v0.1.46, ENG-119)\n\n**What it does**: Global override to treat all rig setup operations as `allowFailure: true`\n\n**Usage**:\n\n```bash\nhankweave --execution ./my-run --ignore-rig-failures\n```\n\n**Use Case**: Resume workflows where rig setup already partially completed\n\n### Directory-Aware Config Resolution (v0.1.46, ENG-139)\n\n**What it does**: Automatically find hank.json in specified directory\n\n**Before**:\n\n```bash\nhankweave ./project/  # Looked in CWD, not ./project/\n```\n\n**After**:\n\n```bash\nhankweave ./project/  # Correctly finds ./project/hank.json\n```\n\n**Behavior**: Data directories containing hank.json are auto-discovered\n\n### Symlink Handling in Output Files (v0.1.46, ENG-125)\n\n**What it does**: Preserve symlinks when copying output files\n\n**Fix**: Added `verbatimSymlinks: true` to `fs.promises.cp()`\n\n**Before**: Copying directories with `node_modules/.bin/` symlinks failed with `EINVAL` errors\n\n**After**: Symlinks preserved correctly during copy operations\n\n### HTML Comment Stripping in Prompts (Unreleased, ENG-158)\n\n**What it does**: Remove HTML comments from prompts before sending to LLM\n\n**Syntax**:\n\n```markdown\nThis instruction is sent to the agent.\n\n<!-- This is a comment for the prompt author, not for the agent.\nIt explains WHY this instruction exists. -->\n\nMore instructions for the agent.\n```\n\n**Behaviors**:\n\n- Comments (`<!-- ... -->`) automatically stripped\n- Trailing newlines consumed to prevent blank line accumulation\n- Applies to system prompts, user prompts, and template variable processing\n- Useful for adding internal notes and documentation\n\n**Philosophy**: \"Prompts - like code - aren't always self-documenting\"\n\n### Output File Conflict Resolution (Unreleased, ENG-115)\n\n**What it does**: Automatic handling of filename collisions when copying output files\n\n**Behavior**:\n\n- Conflicting files renamed with format: `file_<counter>_<timestamp>.ext`\n- Example: `report.pdf` → `report_1_1738678800.pdf`\n- Preflight warnings shown when output directory non-empty\n- Server emits info events with conflict details\n- Safety limit of max 100 conflicts\n\n### Headless Autostart (Unreleased, ENG-180)\n\n**What it does**: Automatically start execution in headless mode without waiting for client\n\n**Behavior**:\n\n- New `requestAutostart()` method for idempotent triggering\n- Prevents race condition where both headless startup and client handshake trigger autostart\n- Smart exit codes: 0 for success/user shutdown, 1 for codon failure\n\n**Use Case**: CI/CD environments, cloud deployments, automated workflows\n\n### Dynamic Port Allocation (Unreleased, ENG-179)\n\n**What it does**: Default to OS-assigned port instead of hardcoded 7777\n\n**Configuration**:\n\n- Default port changed from 7777 to 0 (OS-assigned ephemeral port)\n- Startup sequence reordered: WebSocket binds first, then proxy on `actualPort + 1`\n- Lock file updated with actual ports after binding\n- `start()` method returns actual port\n- Proxy falls back to dynamic port if preferred port unavailable\n\n**Prevents**: Port conflicts when running multiple Hankweave instances\n\n**CLI Help Updated**: Reflects auto-selection behavior\n\n### Cleaner Startup Logs (Unreleased)\n\n**What changed**: Removed noisy debug output from startup\n\n**Before**:\n\n```\n[MODULE] Loading config...\n[MODULE] Initializing runtime...\n[DEBUG] Calculating data signature...\n```\n\n**After**:\n\n```\n╭────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ Hankweave v0.2.0                       │\n│ Platform: darwin-arm64                 │\n│ Node: v20.11.0                         │\n╰────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\nExecution: ~/hanks/my-project\nStatus: resuming\nConfig: hank.json\nClaude SDK: v1.2.3\nCodex SDK: v0.4.5\n```\n\n**Improvements**:\n\n- Version and platform info in clean rounded box\n- Execution info grouped together\n- Paths shortened with `~` for home directory\n- Suppressed verbose \"Calculating data signature...\" message\n- SDK managers return structured info instead of printing directly\n\n---\n\n## Infrastructure & Platform Support\n\n### Windows Support (v0.1.47, PR #77)\n\n**What changed**: Comprehensive Windows compatibility fixes\n\n**Specific Fixes**:\n\n1. **File URL Parsing**: Use `fileURLToPath()` instead of manual parsing for cross-platform paths\n2. **Path Duplication**: Fixed `path.join()` with absolute paths in `HankweaveRuntime` constructor\n3. **Directory Cleanup**: Added `rmSyncWithRetry()` with exponential backoff for Windows file locks\n4. **Build Script**: Replaced Unix commands (`cp -r`, `chmod`) with cross-platform Node.js APIs\n5. **Double Extension**: Prevented `hankweave.exe.exe` on Windows builds\n6. **NPX Discovery**: Set `NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` so npx finds `.npmrc` on Windows\n7. **Codex on Windows**: Guide model to use `Write` tool instead of PowerShell commands\n8. **Line Endings**: `.gitattributes` enforces LF line endings for text files\n\n**Testing**: Full test suite now runs on Windows in CI\n\n### Multi-OS CI Testing (v0.1.47, PR #77)\n\n**What changed**: CI now runs on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows\n\n**Features**:\n\n- E2E tests with retry logic for flaky network conditions\n- Platform-specific test configurations\n- Reusable composite actions:\n  - `setup-environment` - Bun, Node.js, agent auth setup\n  - `dump-test-logs` - Better CI debugging\n- Codex auth via `~/.codex/auth.json` from CI secrets\n- Extended timeouts for slower platforms (Windows)\n\n**Platforms Tested**:\n\n- Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04\n- macOS 13 (Intel), 14 (Apple Silicon)\n- Windows 2022, 2025\n\n### Runtime Extractor Refactor (v0.1.47, PR #77)\n\n**What changed**: Shared utilities for embedded file extraction across all runtime managers\n\n**New Base Extractor** (`runtime-extractor-base.ts`):\n\n- Handles Bun virtual filesystem paths correctly across platforms\n- Shared caching logic\n- Version management\n- Platform detection\n\n**Refactored Extractors**:\n\n- `claude-runtime-extractor.ts`: Migrated to base (-215 lines)\n- `shim-runtime-extractor.ts`: Migrated to base (-186 lines)\n- `codex-runtime-extractor.ts`: New, using base\n\n**Benefits**: Consistency, reduced duplication, easier maintenance\n\n### Public Release Infrastructure (v0.1.41, PR #79)\n\n**What it does**: Automation for maintaining public/private repo split\n\n**Architecture**:\n\n- Two-repo model: private development, public release mirror\n- `hankweave` npm package available publicly\n- Sync workflow transforms private → clean public releases\n- Internal files stripped from public:\n  - `intermediates/` folder\n  - `CLAUDE.md` file\n  - Planning documents\n  - Internal notes\n\n**Scripts**:\n\n- `scripts/sync-public.ts` - Sync and sanitize\n- `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` - Test locally before pushing\n\n**CI Workflow**: `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`\n\n---\n\n## Bug Fixes\n\n### Critical Fixes\n\n#### Dynamic Port Display Bug (Unreleased)\n\n**Problem**: Banner showed `ws://localhost:0` instead of actual assigned port\n**Impact**: TUI attempted to connect to port 0, causing immediate connection failure\n**Fix**: Correctly read actual port from crossws Bun adapter via `.bun.server.port`\n**Affects**: All dynamic port allocations (default behavior)\n\n#### HTTP Request Crash in Headless Mode (Unreleased)\n\n**Problem**: Server crashed when receiving HTTP requests (curl, browser, health checks)\n**Error**: `fetchHandler is not a function`\n**Fix**: Return helpful JSON error message directing users to WebSocket endpoint\n**Impact**: Critical for CI/CD where stray HTTP probes could kill entire runs\n**Added**: CORS headers for better browser compatibility\n\n#### Cost Counting Bug (Post-v0.2.0, ENG-181)\n\n**Problem**: Costs tracked incorrectly in certain scenarios\n**Fix**: Proper cost aggregation and event handling\n**Commit**: 8c2d64b\n\n### Sentinel Fixes\n\n#### Sentinel Output Path Resolution (Unreleased)\n\n**Problem**: Paths with `/` (including `./`) resolved incorrectly\n**Before**: All explicit paths resolved relative to `executionPath` (outer directory)\n**After**: Paths with `/` resolve relative to `agentRootPath` (agent workspace)\n**Behavior**: Filename-only paths still use managed directory: `.hankweave/sentinels/outputs/{id}/`\n**Allows**: Sentinels to write outputs directly to agent workspace (e.g., `./analysis.log`)\n\n### Windows-Specific Fixes (v0.1.47)\n\n1. **Self-test timeout handling**: Improved Windows cleanup and timeout behavior\n2. **Directory cleanup**: Retry logic for Windows file locks\n3. **Path handling**: Prevented Windows path duplication\n4. **Binary extraction**: Detailed logging to diagnose issues\n5. **Unit test failures**: Resolved Windows-specific unit test issues\n6. **Integration test timeouts**: Increased timeouts for slower operations\n\n### Miscellaneous Fixes\n\n#### Loop Expansion with Ignored Early Failures\n\n**Problem**: Loop expansion broke when early codons failed with ignore policy\n**Fix**: Proper handling of ignored failures in loop planning\n\n#### Log Parser Re-parsing Bug\n\n**Problem**: Log parser restarted on each extension, re-processing all previous messages\n**Impact**: Duplicate cost tracking, incorrect state transitions\n**Fix**: Log parser continues running across extensions\n\n#### successResultReceived Reset\n\n**Problem**: Flag not reset between extensions\n**Impact**: Extension failures masked as successes when SDK errors occurred\n**Fix**: Reset flag in `performExtension()` alongside other per-extension state\n\n#### NPX E2E Test Flakiness\n\n**Problem**: Flaky test failures in CI\n**Fix**: Added retry logic (2 attempts), disabled npm update/audit checks\n\n---\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\n### Configuration Schema Changes\n\n#### `recommendations` → `overrides` (v0.1.44, PR #82)\n\n**Breaking**: Renamed field in hank.json\n\n**Before**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"recommendations\": {\n    \"model\": \"claude-opus-4\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**After**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"overrides\": {\n    \"model\": \"claude-opus-4\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Migration**: Update all hank.json files to use `overrides` instead of `recommendations`\n\n#### Checkpoint Directory Rename (v0.2.0)\n\n**Breaking**: Checkpoint git directory renamed\n\n**Before**: `.git`\n**After**: `.hankweavecheckpoints`\n\n**Reason**: Prevent Git submodule detection when committing execution environments\n\n**Migration**: Automatic! Existing execution environments migrated on startup\n\n#### Template Variable Resolution (v0.2.0)\n\n**Breaking**: All template variables now resolve to `agentRoot/`\n\n**Variables Affected**:\n\n- `<%AGENT_ROOT%>`\n- `<%PROJECT_DIR%>`\n- `<%EXECUTION_DIR%>`\n\n**Before**: Mix of resolutions depending on context\n**After**: All consistently resolve to agent workspace\n\n**Impact**: Commands in rigSetup or outputFiles referencing these variables\n\n### Directory Structure Changes (v0.2.0)\n\n**Breaking**: Execution directory now nested\n\n**Before**:\n\n```\nexecution-dir/\n├── .hankweave/\n├── your-files\n└── checkpoints/\n```\n\n**After**:\n\n```\nexecution-dir/\n├── agentRoot/     # Work happens here\n│   └── your-files\n├── rigArchive/    # Archives here\n└── .hankweave/    # System files here\n```\n\n**Migration**: Automatic migration on first v0.2.0 run\n\n**Impact**: External tools referencing execution directory structure\n\n### Deprecated Syntax\n\n#### CLI Flag Syntax (v0.1.34)\n\n**Not Breaking Yet**: Space-separated now preferred\n\n**Old Style** (still supported):\n\n```bash\nhankweave --port=8080 --model=claude-opus-4\n```\n\n**New Style** (recommended):\n\n```bash\nhankweave --port 8080 --model claude-opus-4\n```\n\n**Migration**: Update scripts to use space-separated flags\n**Warning**: Deprecation warnings shown when using `--flag=value` syntax\n\n---\n\n## Configuration & Schema Changes\n\n### New Configuration Fields\n\n#### Codon-Level Fields\n\n**`onFailure`** (v0.2.0):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"onFailure\": {\n    \"action\": \"abort\" | \"retry\" | \"ignore\",\n    \"maxRetries\": 3  // For retry action\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**`exhaustWithPrompt`** (v0.1.46+):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"exhaustWithPrompt\": \"Please continue. Any more?\"\n}\n```\n\n**`archiveOnSuccess`** (v0.2.0):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"archiveOnSuccess\": [\"build/**/*\", \"*.log\"]\n}\n```\n\n#### Hank-Level Fields\n\n**`requirements`** (v0.1.46):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"requirements\": {\n    \"env\": [\"API_KEY\", \"DATABASE_URL\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**`globalSystemPromptFile`** (v0.1.46):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"globalSystemPromptFile\": [\"rules.md\", \"standards.md\"]\n}\n```\n\n**`globalSystemPromptText`** (v0.1.46):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"globalSystemPromptText\": \"Always explain reasoning.\"\n}\n```\n\n**`overrides`** (v0.1.44):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"overrides\": {\n    \"model\": \"claude-opus-4\",\n    \"maxTokens\": 8000\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Schema Files (v0.1.44)\n\nThree JSON Schema files now available:\n\n1. **`schemas/hank.schema.json`**\n   - Defines hank.json structure\n   - Includes all codon fields, loop fields, meta, overrides\n   - Comprehensive descriptions and examples\n\n2. **`schemas/hankweave.schema.json`**\n   - Defines hankweave.json (runtime config)\n   - Includes server settings, environment config\n   - Port, autostart, proxy settings\n\n3. **`schemas/sentinel.schema.json`**\n   - Defines sentinel configuration\n   - Trigger patterns, output handling\n   - Lifecycle and structured output options\n\n### Model Support\n\n**Added**: OpenAI models via Codex\n\n- `gpt-4.1`\n- `gpt-4.1-mini`\n- `gpt-5.2`\n- `gpt-5.2-preview`\n- All o1/o3 models with reasoning effort prefixes (high/xhigh)\n\n**Existing**: Claude models\n\n- `claude-opus-4-20250514`\n- `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`\n- `claude-haiku-4-20250514`\n- etc.\n\n**Existing**: Gemini models\n\n- `gemini-2.5-pro`\n- `gemini-2.5-flash`\n- etc.\n\n---\n\n## CLI & Command Line Interface\n\n### New Flags\n\n**`--attach`** (v0.1.46):\n\n- Connect TUI to running server in read-only mode\n- Example: `hankweave --attach`\n\n**`--ignore-rig-failures`** (v0.1.46):\n\n- Treat all rig setup operations as allowFailure: true\n- Example: `hankweave --execution ./my-run --ignore-rig-failures`\n\n**`--ignore-data-mismatch`** (v0.1.44):\n\n- Resume with changed data without failing\n- Example: `hankweave --execution ./my-run --ignore-data-mismatch --data ./new-data`\n\n**`--version`** (v0.1.38):\n\n- Print version number without banner\n- Example: `hankweave --version`\n\n### Modified Flags\n\n**`--port`** (Unreleased):\n\n- Default changed from 7777 to 0 (dynamic allocation)\n- Explicit port still respected\n\n### Removed Flags\n\n**`-V`** (v0.1.37):\n\n- Removed to avoid confusion with `-v` (validation)\n- Use `--version` instead\n\n### Improved Help Text\n\n**Changes**:\n\n- Better examples for all commands\n- Clearer flag descriptions\n- Positional argument documentation\n- Remote URL usage examples\n- Updated to reflect new features\n\n---\n\n## Developer Experience\n\n### Editor Support (v0.1.44)\n\n**JSON Schema Autocomplete**:\n\n- IntelliSense in VS Code, WebStorm, etc.\n- Hover documentation for all fields\n- Instant validation errors\n- Type-aware suggestions\n\n**Setup**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://unpkg.com/@southbridgeai/hankweave@latest/schemas/hank.schema.json\"\n}\n```\n\n### Better Validation Messages (v0.1.44, PR #80)\n\n**What improved**: Runtime validation error messages\n\n**Before**:\n\n```\nError: Unknown field \"systemPromptFile\"\n```\n\n**After**:\n\n```\nError in codon \"analyze-code\":\n  Unknown field \"systemPromptFile\"\n  Did you mean \"appendSystemPromptFile\"?\n```\n\n**Features**:\n\n- Errors show codon ID and name for context\n- \"Did you mean X?\" suggestions for typos\n- Multiple errors shown together (not just first)\n- Better context for nested errors\n\n### Model Override Actually Works (v0.1.44, PR #81)\n\n**Problem**: `--model` CLI flag didn't actually override codon models\n\n**Fix**: Override applied at config loading before validation\n\n**Before**:\n\n```bash\nhankweave --model claude-opus-4  # Codons still used their configured models\n```\n\n**After**:\n\n```bash\nhankweave --model claude-opus-4  # All codons now use claude-opus-4\n```\n\n### Prompt Documentation (Unreleased, ENG-158)\n\n**Feature**: HTML comments in prompts\n\n**Benefit**: Document WHY instructions exist without sending to LLM\n\n**Example**:\n\n```markdown\nPlease format all code using prettier.\n\n<!-- We require prettier because:\n     1. Team style guide mandates it\n     2. Reduces git diff noise\n     3. Historical context: Added after July 2025 team meeting -->\n\nUse 2-space indentation.\n```\n\n### Lock File Port Discovery (v0.1.46)\n\n**What changed**: Lock file now includes `port` field\n\n**Usage**: `--attach` mode reads port from lock file automatically\n\n**File**: `.hankweave/lock.json`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"pid\": 12345,\n  \"port\": 54321,\n  \"version\": \"0.2.0\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance & Optimization\n\n### Test Runner Optimization (Post-v0.2.0)\n\n**What changed**: New test runner implementation\n\n**Performance**:\n\n- **Before**: 9+ minutes for full test suite\n- **After**: ~3 minutes for full test suite\n- **Improvement**: 3x faster\n\n**Changes**:\n\n- Parallel test execution\n- Better test isolation\n- Reduced setup/teardown overhead\n\n### Gemini Timeout Adjustments (v0.1.46+)\n\n**What changed**: Increased timeouts for Gemini API\n\n**Reason**: Gemini is slower than Claude for some operations\n\n**Impact**: More reliable tests, fewer flaky failures\n\n### Build Performance (v0.1.44)\n\n**What changed**: Schema generation integrated into build\n\n**Process**:\n\n```bash\nbun run generate-schemas  # Auto-generates from Zod\nbun run build            # Builds with fresh schemas\n```\n\n**Benefit**: Schemas always in sync with code\n\n---\n\n## Testing & CI/CD\n\n### E2E Test Coverage\n\n**New Test Suites**:\n\n1. **Failure Policy Tests** (`tests/e2e/test-groups/failure-policy-tests.ts`):\n   - Test abort, retry, ignore policies\n   - Verify state transitions\n   - Check event emissions\n\n2. **Codon Extension Tests** (`tests/e2e/codon-extension-e2e.test.ts`):\n   - Test extension mechanism\n   - Verify single completion event\n   - Test rollback behavior\n   - Validate state management\n\n3. **Codex Integration Tests** (`tests/integration/codex-shim.test.ts`):\n   - Test Codex binary extraction\n   - Verify auth methods\n   - Test self-test functionality\n   - Platform-specific behaviors\n\n4. **Data Mismatch Tests** (`tests/e2e/data-mismatch-ignore-flag-e2e.test.ts`):\n   - Test `--ignore-data-mismatch` flag\n   - Verify data relinking\n   - Check warning messages\n\n### Unit Test Additions\n\n**New Test Files**:\n\n- `tests/unit/codex-runtime-extractor.test.ts` (469 lines)\n- `tests/unit/extension-config.test.ts` (318 lines)\n- `tests/unit/extension-decision.test.ts` (173 lines)\n- `tests/unit/codon-failure-reason.test.ts` (67 lines)\n- `tests/unit/on-failure-config.test.ts` (253 lines)\n- `tests/unit/llm-provider-registry.test.ts` (390 lines)\n- `tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts` (275 lines)\n- `tests/unit/stable-input-path.test.ts` (139 lines)\n- `tests/integration/schema-zod-parity.test.ts` (227 lines)\n\n### CI/CD Improvements\n\n**Platform Matrix**:\n\n- Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04\n- macOS 13 (Intel), 14 (Apple Silicon)\n- Windows Server 2022, 2025\n\n**Reliability**:\n\n- Retry logic for flaky tests\n- Extended timeouts for slow platforms\n- Better log dumping for debugging\n- Conditional test execution per platform\n\n**Workflows**:\n\n- CI on every push/PR to develop and release/alpha\n- Automated schema generation before releases\n- Public sync workflow for release branches\n- Comprehensive E2E, integration, and unit test runs\n\n---\n\n## Behavioral Changes\n\n### Startup Behavior\n\n**Before v0.2.0**:\n\n1. Create execution directory\n2. Start WebSocket server on port 7777\n3. Wait for client to connect and handshake\n4. Autostart after handshake (if enabled)\n\n**After v0.2.0**:\n\n1. Create execution directory with new structure (agentRoot/, rigArchive/, .hankweave/)\n2. Start WebSocket server on dynamic port (or specified port)\n3. In headless mode: autostart immediately\n4. In normal mode: wait for client handshake\n\n### Checkpoint Behavior\n\n**Directory**: Changed from `.git` to `.hankweavecheckpoints`\n\n**Archiving Integration**:\n\n- Rolling back now restores archived files\n- Archive manifest updated during checkpoint operations\n- Empty archive directories cleaned up\n\n### Model Selection\n\n**Override Precedence** (v0.1.44):\n\n1. CLI `--model` flag (highest)\n2. `overrides.model` in hank.json\n3. Codon-specific `model` field\n4. Runtime config `model`\n5. Default model (lowest)\n\n**Previously**: Codon model couldn't be overridden by CLI flag\n\n### Execution Flow\n\n**Extensions** (v0.1.46+):\n\n- Codons with `exhaustWithPrompt` continue until context exhausted\n- Single codon ID throughout (no iteration numbers)\n- Events emitted once at true completion\n- Rollback reverts entire extended codon\n\n**Failure Handling** (v0.2.0):\n\n- Codons can continue after failure based on `onFailure` policy\n- Failed-but-ignored codons don't stop execution\n- Retry policy automatically re-attempts failed codons\n\n### Directory Resolution\n\n**Template Variables** (v0.2.0):\nAll now resolve to `agentRoot/`:\n\n- `<%AGENT_ROOT%>`\n- `<%PROJECT_DIR%>`\n- `<%EXECUTION_DIR%>`\n\n**Config Path Discovery** (v0.1.46):\n\n- `hankweave ./folder/` now correctly looks for `./folder/hank.json`\n- Previously looked in current working directory\n\n### Output Handling\n\n**File Conflicts** (Unreleased):\n\n- Conflicting files automatically renamed with counter and timestamp\n- Preflight warnings for non-empty output directories\n- Info events emitted with conflict details\n\n**Sentinel Outputs** (Unreleased):\n\n- Paths with `/` resolve relative to `agentRoot/`\n- Filename-only paths use managed directory\n\n### Validation Behavior\n\n**Required Environment Variables** (v0.1.46):\n\n- Checked during `--validate` and normal startup\n- Supports `HANKWEAVE_` prefix variants\n- Fails fast with clear error messages\n\n**Schema Validation** (v0.1.44):\n\n- Better error messages with suggestions\n- Multiple errors reported together\n- Context included (codon ID, name)\n\n---\n\n## Summary Statistics\n\n### Version Progression\n\n- **Starting Version**: 0.1.37 (Jan 16, 2026)\n- **Ending Version**: 0.2.0 (Feb 5, 2026)\n- **Major Version Bump**: YES (0.1 → 0.2)\n- **Releases**: 12 releases in ~20 days\n\n### Code Changes\n\n- **Total Commits**: 200+ commits\n- **Major Features**: 15+ features\n- **Bug Fixes**: 50+ fixes\n- **Files Changed**: 500+ files modified/added\n- **Lines of Code**: ~50,000 lines added\n\n### Feature Breakdown\n\n- **Major Features**: 6 (Codex, Failure Handling, Extensions, Directory Separation, JSON Schema, ASCII Viz)\n- **QoL Improvements**: 15+\n- **Infrastructure Improvements**: 5 (Windows support, CI/CD, refactoring, public release)\n- **Bug Fixes**: 50+\n\n### Testing\n\n- **New E2E Tests**: 10+ test suites\n- **New Unit Tests**: 15+ test files\n- **Test Performance**: 3x faster (9min → 3min)\n- **Platform Coverage**: 3 OS, 6 platform variants\n\n### Documentation\n\n- **CHANGELOG Entries**: ~300 lines of changes documented\n- **Planning Documents**: 8 major feature plans\n- **JSON Schemas**: 3 comprehensive schemas\n\n---\n\n## Migration Guide\n\n### Upgrading from v0.1.x to v0.2.0\n\n#### 1. Update Configuration Files\n\n**Rename `recommendations` to `overrides`**:\n\n```bash\n# In all hank.json files:\nsed -i 's/\"recommendations\"/\"overrides\"/g' **/*.json\n```\n\n**Add JSON Schema (optional but recommended)**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://unpkg.com/@southbridgeai/hankweave@latest/schemas/hank.schema.json\",\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n#### 2. Update Scripts\n\n**Change CLI flag syntax**:\n\n```bash\n# Old\nhankweave --port=8080 --model=claude-opus-4\n\n# New\nhankweave --port 8080 --model claude-opus-4\n```\n\n**Update port references**:\n\n- Change hardcoded port 7777 references\n- Use dynamic port discovery or specify explicitly\n\n#### 3. Test Execution\n\n**Run validation first**:\n\n```bash\nhankweave --validate\n```\n\n**Check for directory migration**:\n\n```bash\n# Old structure still works - auto-migrated\nls execution-dir/.git  # Becomes .hankweavecheckpoints\n\n# New structure created automatically\nls execution-dir/agentRoot/\nls execution-dir/rigArchive/\nls execution-dir/.hankweave/\n```\n\n#### 4. Update External Tools\n\n**If accessing execution directory**:\n\n- Update paths from `execution-dir/` to `execution-dir/agentRoot/`\n- System files now in `execution-dir/.hankweave/`\n- Archives in `execution-dir/rigArchive/`\n\n#### 5. Optional: Use New Features\n\n**Add failure handling**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"optional-task\",\n  \"promptFile\": \"task.md\",\n  \"onFailure\": {\n    \"action\": \"ignore\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Add exhaustion extensions**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"exhaustive-task\",\n  \"promptFile\": \"task.md\",\n  \"exhaustWithPrompt\": \"Please continue.\"\n}\n```\n\n**Add archiving**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"build-task\",\n  \"promptFile\": \"build.md\",\n  \"archiveOnSuccess\": [\"build/**/*\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Deprecation Warnings\n\n**Monitor for warnings**:\n\n- `--flag=value` syntax (use `--flag value` instead)\n- Old checkpoint directory (auto-migrated)\n\n### Getting Help\n\n**Documentation**: See updated docs at [docs location]\n**Issues**: Report bugs at [repo URL]\n**Community**: [Discord/forum link if available]\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\nHankweave has undergone significant maturation since January 16, 2026. The jump from v0.1.37 to v0.2.0 represents a major milestone in the project's evolution from prototype to production-ready tool.\n\n### Key Themes\n\n1. **Resilience**: Failure handling and extensions make workflows more robust\n2. **Cross-Platform**: Full Windows, macOS, Linux support\n3. **Developer Experience**: JSON Schema, better validation, cleaner UI\n4. **Flexibility**: Dynamic ports, headless mode, attach mode\n5. **Observability**: Better logging, events, visualization\n\n### Looking Forward\n\nThe v0.2.0 release establishes a solid foundation for:\n\n- More complex agentic workflows\n- Production deployments\n- Team collaboration\n- Cross-platform development\n\nWith comprehensive testing, clear documentation, and robust infrastructure, Hankweave is ready for real-world usage at scale.\n\n---\n\n**Document Version**: 1.0\n**Analysis Date**: February 5, 2026\n**Hankweave Version**: 0.2.0\n**Analysis Scope**: Changes since January 16, 2026\n","numLines":1444,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1444}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:07:17.727Z"}
