chemas/` — for the npm package\n2. `../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/` — for the documentation site's schema hosting\n\nSee `generate-schemas.ts:26-31`:\n```typescript\nconst DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR = path.join(\n  import.meta.dir,\n  \"..\",\n  \"..\",\n  \"hankweave-docs\",\n  \"nextra-site\",\n  \"public\",\n  \"schemas\",\n);\n```\n\nThe script silently skips writing to docs if the path doesn't exist (`docsAvailable` check at line ~77). This relative path hardcodes the assumption that both repos are checked out as siblings. A monorepo would make this relationship explicit and reliable.\n\n---\n\n## Current Release & Sync Pipeline\n\nThe full pipeline is:\n\n```\nSouthBridgeAI/hankweave (private, develop branch)\n    ↓ scripts/release.ts (version bump, changelog, tag)\n    ↓ .github/workflows/release.yml (npm publish @southbridgeai/hankweave, binaries, GH release)\n    ↓ manual trigger: .github/workflows/sync-public.yml\nSouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime (public, release/alpha)\n    ↓ public release.yml (npm publish hankweave, binaries, GH release)\n```\n\nThe docs site is deployed separately to Vercel from `hankweave-docs`.\n\n### Files Stripped Before Public Sync\n\nFrom `scripts/sync-public.ts`:\n- Directories: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`\n- Files: `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `PUBLISHING-PLAN.md`, `telemetry.md`, `scripts/sync-public.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`, `standard-operating-procedures.md`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`\n\nThe `public-release-files/` directory contains replacements overlaid on the public repo:\n- `README.md` (public-facing)\n- `LICENSE.md`, `NOTICE.md`\n- A sanitized `reference/telemetry.md`\n- A simplified `.github/workflows/release.yml`\n\n---\n\n## Monorepo Tooling Research\n\n### Bun Workspaces\n\nBun supports the standard npm workspaces protocol natively. Configuration in root `package.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-project\",\n  \"workspaces\": [\"packages/*\"]\n}\n```\n\nEach package has its own `package.json`. Cross-package references use the `workspace:` protocol:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"pkg-b\": \"workspace:*\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKey features:\n- `bun install` installs all workspaces and de-duplicates dependencies\n- `--filter` flag for running scripts in specific packages\n- `workspace:*` replaced by real version on publish\n- Bun supports full glob syntax including negative patterns\n- **Catalogs**: Share common dependency versions across packages via `catalog:` protocol — define once in root, reference everywhere\n\n**Bun workspaces are likely sufficient for this project** without adding Turborepo, since the project doesn't have many packages and build caching may not be the pain point.\n\n### Turborepo\n\nTurborepo adds task orchestration with caching on top of workspaces:\n- `turbo.json` defines task pipelines and caching rules\n- Tasks can depend on other packages' tasks (`^build` = build dependencies first)\n- Significant speedup for large monorepos via remote caching\n- Incremental adoption possible — can start with one task\n\n**Turborepo may be overkill** for a two-package monorepo. Worth considering if build times become an issue, but adds complexity.\n\n### NX\n\nSimilar to Turborepo but more opinionated. Not evaluated in depth — likely not relevant for this scale.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nBun workspaces alone is the right starting point. The simplicity of two packages (runtime + docs) doesn't warrant additional tooling. Turborepo can be added later if task orchestration and caching becomes needed.\n\n---\n\n## Git History Preservation Options\n\n### git subtree\n\nAllows merging another repo into a subdirectory while preserving its commit history.\n\n```bash\ngit remote add -f hankweave-docs https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs.git\ngit merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories hankweave-docs/main\ngit read-tree --prefix=packages/docs/ -u hankweave-docs/main\ngit commit -m \"Merge hankweave-docs into monorepo\"\n```\n\nFuture syncs: `git pull -s subtree hankweave-docs main`\n\n**Downside**: Can make `git log` noisier. The merged history is preserved but the structure is complex.\n\n### Fresh start\n\nCreate a new repo, copy files, start fresh history. Simpler but loses commit history for both repos.\n\n### git filter-repo / grafting\n\nMore surgical — can rewrite history to place all commits in proper subdirectory paths. More complex.\n\n**Given the project's constraints** (private dev repo, public sanitized mirror), git history preservation is \"nice to have\" but probably less critical than getting the structure right. The public repo already receives snapshots without full history.\n\n---\n\n## Key Considerations for This Migration\n\n### 1. The Public Release Pipeline\n\nThe most complex aspect is the `develop → release/alpha → sync-to-public` pipeline. Key questions to resolve:\n\n- Does the docs repo get a public counterpart too? Currently no.\n- Does the monorepo have a single release cycle, or separate package versions?\n- Does the `sync-public.ts` script need to be aware of multiple packages?\n\n### 2. Schema Coupling\n\n`generate-schemas.ts` already has a cross-repo dependency. In a monorepo, this becomes a proper intra-repo dependency. The `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path would resolve correctly if both repos are under the same root (e.g., `packages/runtime` and `packages/docs`).\n\n### 3. Separate npm Packages\n\nThe runtime publishes as `hankweave` (public) / `@southbridgeai/hankweave` (private). The docs site doesn't publish to npm. This is a \"mixed\" monorepo: one publishable package, one deployable site.\n\n### 4. Vercel Deployment\n\nThe docs site deploys from `hankweave-docs`. Vercel supports monorepos — you specify the root directory for the project. The `vercel.json` in `nextra-site/` would need to be at the monorepo root or Vercel would need to be pointed at the subdirectory.\n\n### 5. CI/CD Changes\n\nThe existing CI workflows are per-repo. In a monorepo:\n- CI would need to run tests only for changed packages (or all)\n- The release workflow for the runtime needs updating\n- The docs build (currently Vercel-managed) would continue on Vercel, but with a new root path\n\n### 6. Biome Scope\n\nCurrent `biome.json` covers `server/**/*`, `tests/e2e/**/*`, `tests/utils/**/*`, `tests/unit/**/*`, `types/**/*`. In a monorepo, this would need to either: be per-package, or be a root config with includes scoped to the runtime package.\n\n### 7. The Internal Strip Requirement\n\nThe release process strips `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `CLAUDE.md`, etc. from the public sync. A monorepo would need to either:\n- Keep the current two-package structure where docs is a separate workspace that doesn't go through the sync\n- Or ensure the sync process still correctly strips the right files\n\n---\n\n## Existing Intermediates That Informed Structure\n\nThe `intermediates/` directory in the hankweave repo contains planning docs for 40+ features. Most are numbered and either single files or multi-phase directories. None appear to relate to monorepo migration specifically.\n\nRelevant to understanding how they work:\n- `standard-operating-procedures.md` section 3 explains intermediates: numbered sequentially, stripped before release, visible only in private dev repo\n\n---\n\n## Source File Locations\n\n| File | Path |\n|------|------|\n| hankweave package.json | `source/hankweave/package.json` |\n| hankweave-docs package.json | `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/package.json` |\n| generate-schemas.ts | `source/hankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts` |\n| release.ts | `source/hankweave/scripts/release.ts` |\n| sync-public.ts | `source/hankweave/scripts/sync-public.ts` |\n| ci.yml | `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/ci.yml` |\n| release.yml | `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/release.yml` |\n| sync-public.yml | `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/sync-public.yml` |\n| biome.json | `source/hankweave/biome.json` |\n| bunfig.toml | `source/hankweave/bunfig.toml` |\n| standard-operating-procedures.md | `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md` |\n| vercel.json | `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/vercel.json` |\n\n---\n\n## Research Links\n\n- [Bun Workspaces documentation](https://bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces)\n- [Bun Catalogs documentation](https://bun.sh/docs/install/catalogs)\n- [Turborepo: adding to existing repo](https://turborepo.dev/repo/docs/getting-started/add-to-existing-repository)\n- [GitHub: git subtree merges](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/using-git/about-git-subtree-merges)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:08:25.181Z"}
